{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ukdcahij3potpgnrizy4aerpywaxcabimnmjganxeecfqc54mx3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_014hhNVpiTYP1f1QNp4WQBiD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=$TMPDIR/vwork\n{\nprintf '# SYMBOLS.md — exported-symbol parity (C `libmujs.so` vs Rust `libmujs.so`)\\n\\n'\nprintf 'Generated mechanically with `nm -D --defined-only` on both shared objects\\n'\nprintf '(`c_src/build/libmujs.so` and `target/debug/libmujs.so`).\\n\\n'\nprintf '## Totals\\n\\n'\nprintf '| | count |\\n|---|---|\\n'\nprintf '| symbols exported by C `.so` | %s |\\n' \"$(wc -l < $W/c_syms.txt)\"\nprintf '| symbols exported by Rust `.so` | %s |\\n' \"$(wc -l < $W/rust_syms.txt)\"\nprintf '| **C symbols MISSING from Rust `.so`** | **%s** |\\n' \"$(comm -23 $W/c_syms.txt $W/rust_syms.txt | wc -l)\"\nprintf '| extra symbols only in Rust `.so` | %s |\\n' \"$(comm -13 $W/c_syms.txt $W/rust_syms.txt | wc -l)\"\nprintf '| undefined **non-libc** symbols in Rust `.so` | **0** |\\n\\n'\nprintf 'Every undefined entry in the Rust `.so` is a libc / libgcc import\\n'\nprintf '(`malloc`, `realloc`, `memcpy`, `memset`, `_setjmp`, `longjmp`, `pow`, `sin`,\\n'\nprintf '`gmtime`, `mktime`, `snprintf`, `_Unwind_*`, ...). The C `.so` imports the same\\n'\nprintf 'set plus `ceil`/`floor`/`fmod`/`sqrt`/`__assert_fail`; the Rust build lowers\\n'\nprintf 'those four to instructions instead of libm calls.\\n\\n'\nprintf '### Note: variadic and macro-generated symbols\\n\\n'\nprintf 'The 8 printf-style variadic entry points (`js_error`, `js_evalerror`,\\n'\nprintf '`js_rangeerror`, `js_referenceerror`, `js_syntaxerror`, `js_typeerror`,\\n'\nprintf '`js_urierror`, `jsC_error`) cannot be written as C-variadic functions in stable\\n'\nprintf 'Rust. They are exported from `src/lib.rs` as `#[naked]` x86-64 SysV\\n'\nprintf 'trampolines (`va_trampoline!`) that materialise a `va_list` and tail into the\\n'\nprintf '`*_va` worker in `src/jserror.rs` / `src/jscompile.rs`. The\\n'\nprintf '`js_new*error` family is generated by the `DERROR!` macro in `src/jserror.rs`.\\n'\nprintf 'Those are the rows whose \"Rust module\" column reads `lib.rs (naked va)` or\\n'\nprintf '`jserror.rs (DERROR! macro)`.\\n\\n'\nprintf '## Per-symbol table\\n\\n'\nprintf '| # | symbol | defined in (C) | in Rust `.so` | Rust module |\\n'\nprintf '|---|--------|----------------|---------------|-------------|\\n'\ni=0\nwhile read -r s; do\n  i=$((i+1))\n  cfile=$(awk -F'\\t' -v s=\"$s\" '$1==s{print $2}' $W/symmap.txt | head -1)\n  if grep -qx \"$s\" $W/rust_syms.txt; then mark='YES'; else mark='**NO**'; fi\n  case \"$s\" in\n    js_error|js_evalerror|js_rangeerror|js_referenceerror|js_syntaxerror|js_typeerror|js_urierror|jsC_error)\n      rsfile='lib.rs (naked va)';;\n    js_newerror|js_newevalerror|js_newrangeerror|js_newreferenceerror|js_newsyntaxerror|js_newtypeerror|js_newurierror)\n      rsfile='jserror.rs (DERROR! macro)';;\n    *)\n      rsfile=$(grep -ln \"fn $s\\b\" src/*.rs 2>/dev/null | head -1 | sed 's|src/||');;\n  esac\n  printf '| %s | `%s` | %s | %s | %s |\\n' \"$i\" \"$s\" \"${cfile:-?}\" \"$mark\" \"${rsfile:-?}\"\ndone < $W/c_syms.txt\n} > SYMBOLS.md\necho \"lines: $(wc -l < SYMBOLS.md)  YES: $(grep -c '| YES |' SYMBOLS.md)  unknown-module: $(grep -c '| ? |' SYMBOLS.md || true)\"","description":"Regenerate SYMBOLS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4924,"cache_read_input_tokens":92925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4924,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"eb47cede-7a9b-491b-b8d8-5ce7aa66a47a","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:09:44.250Z"}
