nuine defects surfaced while enumerating** (recorded as rows 138, 179, 69):\n- `jsstring.c:253` — `Sp_substring_imp` installs `js_try` whose handler does `js_free(J, p)`, but `p` is declared uninitialised at line 228 and is not assigned until line 258. An OOM inside `js_malloc(J, UTFmax + (tail-head))` frees an indeterminate pointer.\n- `jsstring.c:605` — `if (x > 10)` should be `x >= 10`; an out-of-range `$10` back-reference emits `'0' + 10` == `':'`, i.e. `$:` instead of `$10`.\n- `jsobject.c:27` — `Op_toString`'s `switch (self->type)` has no `default`; an unenumerated type pushes nothing and the C-function result is read off the stack top (`this`).\n\n**Two spec deviations in the URI state machines** (rows 247, 252): `Encode` and `Decode` in jsbuiltin.c operate on raw bytes and never validate UTF-8 well-formedness, so the only URIErrors possible are `\"truncated escape sequence\"` (jsbuiltin.c:145) and `\"invalid escape sequence\"` (jsbuiltin.c:149). ES5's lone-surrogate/malformed-sequence URIError paths are absent.\n\n**Also worth flagging for the port:** `S_fromCharCode` (jsstring.c:455) does `js_malloc(J, (top-1) * UTFmax + 1)` with no `JS_STRLIMIT` check and a product that can overflow `int`; and `Sp_split`'s default limit is the magic `1 << 30` (jsstring.c:727, 782) rather than 2^32-1."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":365526,"totalTokens":93262,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":91325,"output_tokens":1488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":115},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":447},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":8,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":8,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":255,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
