{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ExEKVwbb1HAsVuxCMKpJMr","type":"tool_result","content":"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table for `c_src/`\n\nDerived mechanically from the C sources: every `js_*error` / `js_throw` /\n`jsY_error` / `jsP_error` / `jsC_error` / `die()` call site, every `assert()`,\nevery explicit range / bounds / limit check, every NULL check that changes\nbehaviour, and every `return -1` / `return NULL` / `return 0` failure signal.\n\n**Total rows: 933**\n\nThe `cov` column names the Phase-C differential test that constructs the\nexact invalid input, calls BOTH the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`, and asserts\nthey return the SAME error / sentinel. Filled in as tests land.\n\n## Error-surface constants (rejection thresholds)\n\n| constant | value | used as |\n|---|---|---|\n| `JS_STACKSIZE` | 4096 | value-stack overflow -> bare string `\"stack overflow\"` |\n| `JS_ENVLIMIT` | 1024 | env-stack + trace-stack overflow -> `\"stack overflow\"` |\n| `JS_TRYLIMIT` | 64 | try-stack overflow -> bare string `\"exception stack overflow\"` |\n| `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` | 1<<26 | `RangeError \"array too large\"` |\n| `JS_STRLIMIT` | 1<<28 | max string length |\n| `JS_ASTLIMIT` | 400 | `SyntaxError \"too much recursion\"` |\n| `JS_GCFACTOR` | 5.0 | GC trigger threshold |\n| `REG_MAXPROG` | 32768 | `regcomp` error `\"program too large\"` |\n| `REG_MAXREC` | 4096 | `regexec` returns -1 -> `Error \"regexec failed\"` |\n| `REG_MAXCLASS` | 128 | `\"too many character classes\"` |\n| `REG_MAXSPAN` | 64 | `\"too many character class ranges\"` |\n| `REG_MAXSUB` | 16 | `\"too many captures\"` |\n| `REPINF` | 255 | `\"numeric overflow\"` in quantifiers |\n| `maxExponent` (jsdtoa) | 511 | `js_strtod` ERANGE clamp -> inf / 0 |\n\n## Rows\n\n| # | file:line | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | cov |\n|---|-----------|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|-----|\n| 1 | jsrun.c:19 | js_trystackoverflow | try/exception stack full (reached from js_savetry, js_savetrypc, js_ptry when `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` = 64) | pushes JS_TLITSTR then `js_throw`; thrown value is the bare string `\"exception stack overflow\"` (not an Error object) | [ ] |\n| 2 | jsrun.c:27 | js_stackoverflow | value stack or environment stack exhausted (reached from CHECKSTACK and jsR_savescope) | pushes JS_TLITSTR then `js_throw`; thrown value is the bare string `\"stack overflow\"` | [ ] |\n| 3 | jsrun.c:35 | js_outofmemory | allocation failure or memlimit exceeded (reached from js_malloc / js_realloc) | pushes JS_TLITSTR then `js_throw`; thrown value is the bare string `\"out of memory\"` | [ ] |\n| 4 | jsrun.c:43 | js_runlimit | instruction budget exhausted (reached from jsR_run) | pushes JS_TLITSTR then `js_throw`; thrown value is the bare string `\"script ran too long\"` | [ ] |\n| 5 | jsrun.c:56 | js_malloc | `J->memlimit > 0 && size >= J->memlimit` | js_outofmemory → throws `\"out of memory\"` | [ ] |\n| 6 | jsrun.c:61 | js_malloc | host allocator `J->alloc(J->actx, NULL, size)` returns NULL | js_outofmemory → throws `\"out of memory\"`; would `return NULL` if throw ever returned | [ ] |\n| 7 | jsrun.c:70 | js_realloc | `J->memlimit > 0 && size >= J->memlimit` | js_outofmemory → throws `\"out of memory\"` | [ ] |\n| 8 | jsrun.c:75 | js_realloc | host allocator returns NULL on resize | js_outofmemory → throws `\"out of memory\"` | [ ] |\n| 9 | jsrun.c:106 | CHECKSTACK (macro) | `TOP + n >= JS_STACKSIZE` (JS_STACKSIZE == 4096) | js_stackoverflow → throws `\"stack overflow\"` | [ ] |\n......\n| 930 | utf.c:270 | isupperrune | `c` not found in the `ucd_tolower*` tables | returns 0 | [ ] |\n| 931 | utf.c:284 | isalpharune | `c` not found in `ucd_alpha2`/`ucd_alpha1` | returns 0 | [ ] |\n| 932 | utf.c:294 | tolowerrune_full | `c` has no full-lowercase mapping (`!p \\|\\| c != p[0]`) | returns `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 933 | utf.c:305 | toupperrune_full | `c` has no fu