s which representation is used --\n    this is a REAL input-shape axis: strings shorter than the shrstr capacity\n    are stored inline)\n  - `js_pushlstring` with embedded NUL bytes and with n = 0\n  - object creation: js_newobject/js_newobjectx/js_newarray/js_newboolean/\n    js_newnumber/js_newstring/js_newcfunction/js_newcfunctionx/\n    js_newcconstructor/js_newuserdata/js_newuserdatax\n  - property API: js_get/set/def/del/hasproperty, js_defaccessor,\n    js_get/set/has/delindex, js_get/setlength, with the JS_READONLY /\n    JS_DONTENUM / JS_DONTCONF attribute cross-product, on plain objects vs\n    arrays vs strings vs functions vs userdata\n  - ARRAY REPRESENTATION: grep `simple` / `flat` in jsrun.c/jsvalue.c/\n    jsproperty.c. Arrays have TWO internal representations (flat/simple vs\n    hashed property list) and `jsR_unflattenarray` converts. Enumerate the\n    shapes that hit each: dense append, sparse write, delete, length shrink,\n    non-index property on an array.\n  - iterators: js_pushiterator/js_nextiterator with own = 0 vs 1, over objects\n    with/without prototype chain properties, over arrays (flat and unflattened)\n  - conversions: js_toboolean/tonumber/tostring/tointeger/toint32/touint32/\n    toint16/touint16/typeof/type/repr and the try* variants, over EVERY value\n    tag (undefined, null, boolean, number, shrstr, litstr, memstr, object,\n    array, function, cfunction, userdata, regexp, Date, Number/String/Boolean\n    wrapper objects)\n  - `js_compare` / `js_equal` / `js_strictequal` / `js_instanceof` / `js_concat`\n    over the type cross-product\n  - `js_ref` / `js_unref` / registry / global accessors\n  - GC: `js_gc(J, report)` with report 0 vs 1; gcthresh growth\n\nWrite ONE ROW PER MEANINGFUL COMBINATION the C actually distinguishes (the\ncross-product of the axes, pruned to what the code really branches on).\n\nOutput format — write ONLY the markdown table rows (no header, no preamble) to:\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/configs_g1.md\n\nEach row must be exactly:\n| N | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n\n  - N sequential starting at 1\n  - entry point(s) = the exported C function(s) the row drives, e.g.\n    `js_pushlstring + js_tostring`\n  - configuration = precise option settings AND input shape, e.g.\n    `flags=JS_STRICT; string of 7 bytes (JS_TSHRSTR inline representation)`\n\nBe exhaustive but non-redundant. I expect 120-200 rows. Derive rows from what the\nC branches on -- read the code, do not guess.\n\nVerify at the end: run `wc -l` and `grep -c '^|'` on the output file and report\nboth numbers plus the row count. Do NOT modify anything under c_src/."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2031,"cache_read_input_tokens":115753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2031,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"4194e100-59c4-4090-9286-906a9cd07034","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:25:04.660Z"}
