js_newregexp(J, pat, flags)` | cross-product of `JS_REGEXP_G`, `JS_REGEXP_I`, `JS_REGEXP_M` (8 combos) |\\n'\nprintf '| regexp compile flags | `js_regcomp` / `js_regcompx` `cflags` | `0`, `REG_ICASE`, `REG_NEWLINE`, both |\\n'\nprintf '| regexp exec flags | `js_regexec` `eflags` | `0`, `REG_NOTBOL` (merged with `prog->flags`) |\\n'\nprintf '| regexp captures out | `js_regexec` `sub` | `NULL` / real `Resub` (nsub 0..`REG_MAXSUB`=16) |\\n'\nprintf '| radix | `js_strtol` | 0, 1, 2..36 |\\n'\nprintf '| lexer mode | `jsY_lex` vs `jsY_lexjson` | JS vs JSON token grammar |\\n\\n'\nprintf '### Input-shape axes the code special-cases\\n\\n'\nprintf '| axis | distinct shapes |\\n|---|---|\\n'\nprintf '| string representation | `JS_TSHRSTR` (inline, n <= 15), `JS_TLITSTR` (borrowed literal), `JS_TMEMSTR` (heap `js_String`) |\\n'\nprintf '| value tag | undefined, null, boolean, number, shrstr, litstr, memstr, object |\\n'\nprintf '| object class | `JS_COBJECT`, `JS_CARRAY`, `JS_CFUNCTION`, `JS_CSCRIPT`, `JS_CCFUNCTION`, `JS_CERROR`, `JS_CBOOLEAN`, `JS_CNUMBER`, `JS_CSTRING`, `JS_CREGEXP`, `JS_CDATE`, `JS_CMATH`, `JS_CJSON`, `JS_CARGUMENTS`, `JS_CITERATOR`, `JS_CUSERDATA` |\\n'\nprintf '| array representation | `simple` (flat) vs unflattened hashed property tree; the conversion triggers |\\n'\nprintf '| stack index sign | positive (from `bot`) vs negative (from `top`) |\\n'\nprintf '| argument count | 0, 1, many; fewer / more than declared arity |\\n'\nprintf '| UTF-8 width | 1, 2, 3, 4 byte sequences; boundary runes 0x7F/0x80/0x7FF/0x800/0xFFFF/0x10000/0x10FFFF; surrogates; overlong; truncated |\\n'\nprintf '| double shape | 0, -0, subnormal, integral, needs-17-digits, inf, nan, INT_MIN/INT_MAX/UINT_MAX, 2^31, 2^32, 2^53 |\\n'\nprintf '| number->string form | fixed vs exponential: exponential iff `point < -5 \\\\|\\\\| point > 21`; exact-int `js_itoa` fast path |\\n'\nprintf '| empty / one / many | 0-length strings and arrays, single element, many elements |\\n\\n'\nprintf '## Rows\\n\\n'\nprintf '| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | cov |\\n'\nprintf '|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\\n'\nn=0\nfor g in configs_g1.md configs_g2.md; do\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    case \"$line\" in '|'*) ;; *) continue;; esac\n    n=$((n+1))\n    rest=${line#*|}; rest=${rest#*|}\n    printf '| %s |%s\\n' \"$n\" \"$rest\"\n  done < $W/$g\ndone\n} > CONFIGS.md\necho \"CONFIGS.md: $(wc -l < CONFIGS.md) lines, $(grep -cE '^\\| [0-9]+ \\|' CONFIGS.md) numbered rows, $(grep -c '\\[ \\] |$' CONFIGS.md) unchecked\"","description":"Assemble CONFIGS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":125866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":813,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"f80077ba-bec0-42da-a8c1-b3926f47e857","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:40:53.298Z"}
