{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3cliednllvnnnt2dhcct76emrcm6lj7vpkagnkmbgawahbgofysq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_015AApqykkz5isZd8Dkoao7h","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write api_state differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Work in /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust\n\nCONTEXT\nThis is a C->Rust translation of MuJS being verified by DIFFERENTIAL TESTING.\n`c_src/` holds the C ground truth (READ-ONLY, NEVER MODIFY, and never write any\nnew file anywhere under c_src/). `src/*.rs` is the Rust translation, built as a\ncdylib. A test harness already exists at `tests/common/mod.rs` which dlopens\nBOTH `c_src/build/libmujs.so` and `target/debug/libmujs.so` and exposes every\nexported symbol as a method. Existing passing examples you MUST read first for\nstyle: `tests/ll_num.rs`, `tests/ll_regexp.rs`, `tests/ll_lex.rs`, `tests/smoke.rs`.\n\nHARNESS API (in tests/common/mod.rs -- read it, it is ~1250 lines)\n  libs() -> &'static Pair          // Pair { c: Lib, rs: Lib }\n  Lib has an `unsafe fn` per exported symbol, e.g.\n      l.js_newstate(alloc, actx, flags) -> JS\n      l.js_pcall(j, n) -> c_int ; l.js_ploadstring(j, file, src) -> c_int\n      l.js_gettop(j), l.js_pop(j,n), l.js_pushnumber(j,x), ...\n      l.pred(\"js_isarray\", j, idx) -> c_int      // generic (JS,int)->int\n      l.nullary(\"js_dup\", j) / l.nullary_i(\"js_equal\", j)\n      l.newerror(\"js_newtypeerror\", j, msg)\n  new_state(l, flags) -> JS        // installs report hook + `print`/`dump` globals\n  set_cur(l)                       // MUST be called before entering a library\n                                   // whenever a callback (print/report) can fire\n  eval(l, flags, src) -> EvalResult { load_rc, call_rc, result, out, top }\n  dostring(l, flags, src) -> (c_int, String)\n  diff_eval(flags, src) / diff_dostring(flags, src)   // assert C == Rust\n  out_clear() / out_push(bytes) / out_take() -> String\n  cstr(&str) -> CString ; from_c(*const c_char) -> String\n  Rng::new(seed) with .next_u32/.below/.range/.f64_sane/.f64_any/\n      .ascii_string/.unicode_string/.raw_bytes\n  with_big_stack(fn_item)          // run a test body on a 512MB stack; REQUIRED\n                                   // for anything with deep recursion\n\nYOUR TASK\nCreate ONE new file `tests/api_state.rs` with differential tests covering the\nrows of `CONFIGS.md` in the ranges 1-40 and 183-197, i.e.:\n  - js_newstate: flags 0 vs JS_STRICT; custom js_Alloc with a non-NULL actx;\n    an allocator that returns NULL on the Nth call (must produce the same\n    failure/NULL-state behaviour in both); js_newstate returning NULL.\n  - js_setlimit(J, runlimit, memlimit): the 2x2 of zero/nonzero, plus a runlimit\n    small enough to trigger `\"script ran too long\"` and a memlimit small enough\n    to trigger `\"out of memory\"` -- assert BOTH libraries produce the identical\n    report text and return code.\n  - js_setreport with a custom hook, with NULL, and never called.\n  - js_atpanic: assert the returned OLD handler is non-NULL in both, and install\n    a custom panic handler.\n  - js_setcontext / js_getcontext round-trip.\n  - js_loadstring vs js_loadeval vs js_ploadstring vs js_dostring, and js_eval:\n    the `iseval` axis (which strictness and which scope is captured). Compare\n    behaviour of `eval(\"var x=1\")` vs a plain script, in strict and non-strict\n    mode, including indirect eval.\n  - js_call vs js_pcall vs js_construct vs js_pconstruct with n = 0,1,2,many and\n    n different from the callee's declared arity; callee = JS function, C\n    function (js_newcfunction), C constructor (js_newcconstructor), a\n    non-callable value, a script.\n  - js_ref / js_unref / js_getregistry / js_setregistry / js_delregistry and\n    js_getglobal / js_setglobal / js_defglobal / js_delglobal, including\n    js_defglobal with each combination of JS_READONLY|JS_DONTENUM|JS_DONTCONF.\n  - js_gc(J, report) with report 0 and 1, called repeatedly, with live and dead\n    objects, and after creating many objects (exercise gcthresh growth).\n    NOTE: js_gc(J,1) prints its report via printf to stdout, and jsgc.c:255\n    divides by ntot -- read the C first and only test what is well-defined.\n  - js_currentfunction / js_currentfunctiondata via a js_newcfunctionx with a\n    data pointer and a finalizer.\n  - js_newuserdata / js_newuserdatax with has/put/del/finalize hooks: assert the\n    hooks fire in the same order with the same arguments in both libraries\n    (record calls into a Vec via the harness out_push mechanism).\n  - js_savetry/js_endtry/js_throw reachable state: the try-stack limit\n    JS_TRYLIMIT=64 -> the bare string \"exception stack overflow\" (drive it by\n    nesting 70+ JS try/catch blocks or 70 nested js_pcall levels).\n\nRULES\n  - Every call must go through the harness (i.e. through the .so exports).\n    Never call Rust functions directly.\n  - Use MANY randomized inputs per row with a FIXED seed, not one hand-picked\n    value.\n  - Compare byte-for-byte: return codes, output text, error messages, js_gettop.\n  - NEVER call a throwing entry point outside a protected context\n    (js_pcall/js_pconstruct/js_ploadstring/js_dostring/js_try*). Doing so\n    longjmps out of your test and corrupts the process.\n  - If a test needs deep recursion, wrap it: `#[test] fn t_x(){ with_big_stack(body_t_x); } fn body_t_x(){...}`\n  - Some C paths are UNDEFINED BEHAVIOUR (out-of-bounds writes, running off the\n    end of a buffer). If you find one, do NOT test it; instead add a `///`\n    comment naming the file:line and why it is not differentially testable.\n    Check the C source before assuming.\n  - Keep each individual test under ~60s. Use `timeout 600 cargo test\n    --no-default-features --test api_state` to run.\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE\nThe C is ALWAYS right. Fix `src/*.rs`. Use the Edit tool for surgical changes --\ndo NOT use Write on any existing file under src/ (another agent may be editing a\ndifferent function in the same file). Re-read the corresponding C function and\nmake the Rust match it exactly. Report every divergence you found and fixed.\n\nFINISH ONLY WHEN `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test api_state`\npasses with 0 failures. Report: the number of tests, the number of CONFIGS rows\ncovered, and every divergence found+fixed (with file:line). If you could not make\nsomething pass, say so explicitly rather than deleting the test."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":418,"cache_read_input_tokens":188121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":418,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"688b8a9c-8e65-4318-a173-61bbc495573d","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:07.774Z"}
