{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EMf6eEVS5a2rUMnx8z3nby","type":"tool_result","content":"136\t\n137\t/* ------------------------------------------------------- date warm-up ---- */\n138\t\n139\t/// `LocalTZA()` in jsdate.c caches its result in a function-static on first\n140\t/// call, and computes it with `gmtime()`/`localtime()`, which share one static\n141\t/// `struct tm` inside libc.  cargo runs #[test]s on parallel threads, so if two\n142\t/// tests raced into the *first* LocalTZA call of the C library and of the Rust\n143\t/// library the two caches could be seeded from interleaved `struct tm` data and\n144\t/// end up different.  Force both caches to be filled once, single-threaded.\n145\t///\n146\t/// TZ is deliberately NOT modified: both libraries live in the same process and\n147\t/// therefore already see the same zone.  On a UTC host that means LocalTime()\n148\t/// == identity, so fmttime's `tza < 0` / `tza > 0` branches are only reachable\n149\t/// when the host zone is not UTC; the `tza == 0` branch is always covered\n150\t/// through Dp_toUTCString/Dp_toISOString, which pass 0 explicitly.\n151\tfn warm_dates() {\n152\t    static W: OnceLock<()> = OnceLock::new();\n153\t    W.get_or_init(|| {\n154\t        let p = libs();\n155\t        for l in [&p.c, &p.rs] {\n156\t            unsafe {\n157\t                out_clear();\n158\t                let j = new_state(l, 0);\n159\t                let cs = cstr(\"'' + new Date(0); new Date(0).getTimezoneOffset()\");\n160\t                l.js_dostring(j, cs.as_ptr());\n161\t                l.js_freestate(j);\n162\t                let _ = out_take();\n163\t            }\n164\t        }\n165\t    });\n166\t}\n167\t\n168\t/* --------------------------------------- low level js_newregexp runner --- */\n169\t\n170\t#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\n171\tstruct Run {\n172\t    rc: c_int,\n173\t    out: String,\n174\t    top: c_int,\n175\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SSnq5WCrbjCp3GLxjJr9Qz","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"821f7380-1c0b-48ee-8d42-89b1166bef2a","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:39:40.002Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write js_builtins differential tests"}
