{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a9f3c7aa379af7bd5","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SSnq5WCrbjCp3GLxjJr9Qz","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-0eE2Fw-translated-rust/a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2/tasks/a9f3c7aa379af7bd5.output","summary":"All done. Final verification passes.\n\n## Result\n\n`timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test js_builtins` → **35 tests, 0 failures, ~5 s** (also verified 3× consecutively and under `--test-threads=1`). The whole repo suite still passes: 114 tests across 7 binaries (`api_state` 42, `js_builtins` 35, `ll_lex` 8, `ll_num` 10, `ll_regexp` 8, `ll_utf` 7, `smoke` 4).\n\nNew file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/js_builtins.rs` (~2700 lines, ~110k generated JS statements from fixed seeds). Nothing under `src/` or `tests/common/` was touched.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed\n\n**None.** The Rust translation matched the C byte-for-byte (return code, output text, error messages, `js_gettop`, result repr) on every case, including the C quirks the task called out, which I verified are actually reached:\n- `jsstring.c:605` `if (x > 10)` → `'ab'.replace(/(a)/,'$10')` yields `\"$:b\"` in both.\n- `jsdate.c:748` `Dp_setUTCHours` defaulting minutes from `HourFromTime` → `new Date(7h33m).setUTCHours(5)` gives `05:07:00` in both.\n- `js_Regexp::last` is `unsigned short` → `lastIndex = 70000` reads back `4464`, `-1` reads back `65535`.\n- `Math.round(-0.3)` returns **+0** (C's `return -0` is an int constant).\n- `String.fromCharCode(0)` → overlong NUL, length 1; `fromCharCode(0x80000000)` → length 0.\n\n## CONFIGS.md rows covered\n\n90, 98, 116, 118–121, 152, 285–306, 404–450. **Note:** the task's stated ranges don't match the current `CONFIGS.md` — rows 88–110 there are `js_get/set/defproperty` and 207–253 are raw `js_regcomp` shapes (already covered by `ll_regexp.rs`). I covered the rows matching the task's *content* description, listed in the file's module header.\n\n## C undefined behaviour found and excluded (documented with `///`)\n\n- **`c_src/src/jsstring.c:573`** — `Sp_replace_regexp`'s *function*-replacement arm does `for (x = 0; m.sub[x].sp; ++x)`, relying on a NULL terminator that only exists because `regexec` clears all `REG_MAXSUB`==16 slots. A regexp with the maximum 15 capture groups where **all** participate fills `sub[0..15]`, so it reads `m.sub[16]` — past the end of the stack-local `Resub` — and pushes a garbage pointer. **Both `libmujs.so` builds SIGSEGV on it** (I hit it, isolated it to each library separately, then capped that variant at 13 groups). All other capture walks (`Sp_split_regexp`, `js_RegExp_prototype_exec`, the string-replacement arm) are bounded by `m.nsub` and are tested up to 15 groups.\n- **`c_src/src/jsarray.c:279`, `:365`** — `Ap_sort_cmp`/`Ap_sort_swap` read `u.a.simple`/`u.a.array` without checking the object class, so `Array.prototype.sort.call(nonArray, …)` reads a never-stored union member.\n- **`c_src/src/jsstring.c:253-258`** — `Sp_substring_imp`'s `js_try` handler frees `p` before it is assigned (OOM-only).\n- **`c_src/src/jsdate.c:319-347`** — `fmtdate`/`fmttime` convert a NaN time to `int` and overflow `365*(y-1970)` *before* the `isfinite` guard; results are discarded and `d2i` in `src/jsi.rs` already reproduces gcc's `cvttsd2si`, so the invalid-date path is tested.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **The batch helper is hardened against vacuous passes.** My first version had 4 tests whose generated scripts contained syntax errors (e.g. `.split(, 0)`, `.slice(1, )`, `JSON.parse(''a'')`); both libraries reported the identical syntax error, so the batches \"passed\" without executing anything. `diff_lines_n` now asserts `load_rc == 0`, `call_rc == 0` and a floor on emitted output lines, which surfaced all four; they are fixed.\n2. **TZ is pinned once, process-wide** (`XYZ5:30`, offset +330 min) inside a `OnceLock` before either library caches `LocalTZA`, with an assertion that both libraries agree. Without it a UTC host leaves `LocalTime()`/`UTC()`/`getTimezoneOffset` and `fmttime`'s signed-offset arm completely untested. `fmttime`'s `tza > 0` arm is unreachable from a single process (the only non-zero `tza` any caller passes is the once-cached `LocalTZA()`), which is noted in the file. The warm-up also removes a pre-existing latent race: `LocalTZA` uses `gmtime`/`localtime`, which share one static `struct tm` in libc, so two parallel tests seeding the two libraries' caches could have produced different offsets.","usage":{"total_tokens":328856,"tool_uses":106,"duration_ms":2226051},"uuid":"5a7eb384-6f54-4098-b732-b6e7cd60917a","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2"}
