{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_im6ksngpc4iq6hq4opa5khcu36kvabzs4nk5k2q22xywcviubd6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019QRhGRL5oyKghdRTM5wVAm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write api_stack differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Work in /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust\n\nCONTEXT\nC->Rust translation of MuJS, verified by DIFFERENTIAL TESTING against the C.\n`c_src/` is the ground truth: READ-ONLY, never modify it and never create any\nfile under it. `src/*.rs` is the Rust translation built as a cdylib.\n\nCRITICAL BUILD RULE\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib (the tests reach it only via dlopen).\nALWAYS run `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test api_stack` -- that script builds\nthe cdylib, stamps a source hash, then runs cargo test. If you run bare\n`cargo test` after editing src/, the harness will abort with a \"STALE Rust\ncdylib\" assertion. Never bypass that assertion.\n\nREAD FIRST\n  tests/common/mod.rs           - the harness (~1350 lines)\n  tests/api_state.rs            - a large existing example in exactly the style wanted\n  tests/gaps.rs                 - shows protected-call probes + stdout capture\n  CONFIGS.md                    - the configuration-surface table\n\nHARNESS API\n  libs() -> &'static Pair { c: Lib, rs: Lib }\n  Lib has an `unsafe fn` per exported symbol; plus generic helpers:\n      l.pred(\"js_isarray\", j, idx) -> c_int          // (JS,int)->int\n      l.nullary(\"js_dup\", j) / l.nullary_i(\"js_equal\", j)\n      l.raw2::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)>(\"name\")    // arbitrary signature\n  new_state(l, flags) -> JS      // installs report hook + `print`/`dump` globals\n  set_cur(l)                     // call before entering a library (callbacks)\n  eval / dostring / diff_eval / diff_dostring\n  cstr / from_c / out_clear / out_take\n  Rng::new(seed): next_u32/below/range/f64_sane/f64_any/ascii_string/\n                  unicode_string/raw_bytes\n  with_big_stack(fn_item)        // 512MB stack for deep recursion\n\nYOUR TASK\nCreate ONE new file `tests/api_stack.rs` covering CONFIGS.md rows 41-70 and\n142-182, i.e. the stack API, the value pushes, and every conversion /\ncomparison. Specifically:\n\n1. STACK API: js_gettop, js_pop, js_rot, js_copy, js_remove, js_insert,\n   js_replace, js_dup, js_dup2, js_rot2, js_rot3, js_rot4, js_rot2pop1,\n   js_rot3pop2. Drive them as RANDOMISED OPERATION SEQUENCES: build a stack of\n   known values, apply a random sequence of 20-80 operations with random\n   (positive AND negative, in-range AND out-of-range) indices, and after EVERY\n   step compare the ENTIRE observable stack contents (js_gettop plus js_type /\n   js_typeof / js_tryrepr at every index) between C and Rust. Use a fixed seed\n   and many sequences.\n   IMPORTANT: `js_insert` is unconditionally `js_error(J, \"not implemented yet\")`\n   (jsrun.c:424) -- verify BOTH libraries throw the identical error, and note\n   that it must be called inside a protected call.\n   IMPORTANT: read `stackidx` in jsrun.c first to learn exactly which indices are\n   valid and what happens for out-of-range ones; some out-of-range values are\n   UB (reads outside the stack array). Test only the well-defined ones and add a\n   `///` comment for the rest naming file:line.\n\n2. PUSHES + STRING REPRESENTATION: js_pushundefined/null/boolean/number/string/\n   lstring/literal/global, js_newobject/newobjectx/newarray/newboolean/\n   newnumber/newstring. Cover the JS_TSHRSTR (n <= 15 inline) vs JS_TLITSTR vs\n   JS_TMEMSTR axis: read jsrun.c js_pushstring/js_pushlstring/js_pushliteral and\n   jsvalue.c js_newstring to find the exact length thresholds (they differ!), and\n   test lengths on both sides of each. Include embedded NUL bytes and n = 0.\n   Also push booleans with values other than 0/1 (js_pushboolean takes any int).\n\n3. CONVERSIONS over EVERY value shape: js_toboolean, js_tonumber, js_tostring,\n   js_tointeger, js_toint32, js_touint32, js_toint16, js_touint16, js_typeof,\n   js_type, js_repr, js_torepr, and the try* variants js_trystring/js_trynumber/\n   js_tryinteger/js_tryboolean/js_tryrepr. The value shapes must include:\n   undefined, null, true, false, +0, -0, NaN, +-Infinity, integers, fractions,\n   huge/subnormal doubles, short strings, long strings, numeric strings,\n   plain objects, arrays (empty/dense/sparse), functions, C functions, userdata,\n   regexps, Dates, and Number/String/Boolean wrapper objects. Build the values by\n   evaluating a JS expression and leaving the result on the stack, then call each\n   conversion at that index. Randomise the doubles and strings with a fixed seed.\n   NOTE: js_tostring on a number and js_toobject on a primitive MUTATE the stack\n   slot in place -- assert that the post-call stack state matches too.\n   NOTE: the try* variants return a default on throw; construct throwing values\n   (e.g. `{toString:function(){throw 1}}`) and check both return the default.\n\n4. PREDICATES: js_isdefined/isundefined/isnull/isboolean/isnumber/isstring/\n   isprimitive/isobject/isarray/isregexp/iscoercible/iscallable/iserror/\n   isnumberobject/isstringobject/isbooleanobject/isdateobject, and\n   js_isuserdata with a matching tag, a non-matching tag, and a NULL tag, over\n   the same full set of value shapes AND at out-of-range indices.\n\n5. COMPARISONS: js_compare (check the `okay` out-parameter too), js_equal,\n   js_strictequal, js_instanceof, js_concat over the CROSS PRODUCT of the value\n   shapes (at least ~40x40). js_instanceof throws for a non-callable right-hand\n   side -- do it in a protected call.\n\n6. js_currentfunction / js_currentfunctiondata at top level (BOT == 0) and\n   inside a C function.\n\nRULES\n  - Every call must go through the harness (i.e. through the .so exports).\n    Never call Rust functions directly.\n  - MANY randomized inputs per row, fixed seed. Not one hand-picked value.\n  - Compare byte-for-byte, including js_gettop after every operation.\n  - NEVER call a throwing entry point outside a protected context\n    (js_pcall/js_pconstruct/js_ploadstring/js_dostring). It longjmps out of your\n    test and corrupts the process. Use the cfunction-probe pattern from\n    tests/gaps.rs (`newregexp_probe`) for anything that can throw.\n  - Some C paths are UNDEFINED BEHAVIOUR. Do NOT test those; add a `///` comment\n    naming file:line and why. Check the C source before assuming.\n  - Keep each test under ~60s.\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE\nThe C is ALWAYS right. Fix `src/*.rs` with the Edit tool (surgical edits only --\ndo NOT use Write on any existing file under src/, another agent may be editing a\ndifferent function in the same file). Re-read the C function and make the Rust\nmatch exactly.\n\nFINISH ONLY WHEN `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test api_stack` passes with 0\nfailures, run 2x to confirm it is not flaky. Report: number of tests, CONFIGS\nrows covered, and every divergence found+fixed with file:line. If something\ncannot pass, say so explicitly rather than deleting the test."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1748,"cache_read_input_tokens":307624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1748,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"30e1643a-8e77-426a-aac8-ecb81812b607","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:36:09.924Z"}
