{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014WZsePgrsgKEY9PFj12Zu8","type":"tool_result","content":"110:/// A `js_Alloc` that (a) proves `actx` is threaded through untouched,\n111:/// (b) counts every allocating / freeing call so leaks can be compared, and\n112:/// (c) can be made to return NULL on exactly the Nth allocating call.\n113:unsafe extern \"C\" fn tracking_alloc(\n157:/// Run `f` against the C library and then the Rust library, wrapping each run\n158:/// in a fresh output buffer, and assert the two transcripts are byte-identical.\n159:fn diff2(tag: &str, f: impl Fn(&Lib) -> String) -> String {\n177:/// Snapshot of the top of the stack plus the frame size.\n187:/// Describe the top of the stack without going through any `js_try`-based\n188:/// helper.  `js_tryrepr` (jsrepr.c:275) has *no* `js_ptry` guard, so calling it\n189:/// at `trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` throws into the enclosing frame; the try-limit\n190:/// tests must therefore inspect values with these non-throwing accessors only.\n203:/// `js_ref` renders an object as `\"%p\"` of its address (jsrun.c:949), which is\n204:/// necessarily different in the two processes' heaps.  Replace it with a stable\n205:/// token so the rest of the transcript can still be compared byte-for-byte.\n206:fn norm_ref(name: &str) -> String {\n214:/// Pop back down to `base` without ever asking `js_pop` for more than there is\n215:/// (`js_pop` past the frame raises js_error \"stack underflow!\").\n223:/// `js_ploadstring` + `js_pcall` of an expression, leaving its value on the\n224:/// stack.  Returns the composite return code.\n237:/// Records the frame it was called in, then returns a string.\n238:unsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_probe(j: JS) {\n254:/// Pushes nothing at all (row 26: TOP == save_top -> undefined result).\n255:unsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_void(j: JS) {\n260:/// Pushes three values (row 26: only the topmost survives).\n261:unsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_three(j: JS) {\n269:/// A C const