{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_eple7sdpvtgjj5o2q2rmyzva5ikhnsr6ke6ryar5qsspdmkzroja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fw1BTdwRDLaYrrQtBZEZoY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/api_stack.rs","content":"//! Differential coverage for CONFIGS.md rows 41-70 (the stack API and every\n//! value push) and rows 142-182 (every conversion, predicate and comparison).\n//!\n//! Everything goes through the two `libmujs.so` exports; nothing calls into the\n//! Rust crate directly.\n//!\n//! # What is deliberately NOT tested (undefined behaviour in the C)\n//!\n//! * `js_pop(J, n)` with `n < 0` (jsrun.c:403) raises TOP above the live part of\n//!   the value stack; the slots above the old TOP were never initialised, so\n//!   every later `stackidx` read is a read of uninitialised memory.\n//! * `js_dup`/`js_dup2`/`js_rot2`/`js_rot3`/`js_rot4`/`js_rot2pop1`/`js_rot3pop2`\n//!   (jsrun.c:442-497) and `js_rot(J, n)` with `n > js_gettop()` (jsrun.c:498)\n//!   have no bounds check whatsoever. At top level BOT is 0, so a frame with\n//!   fewer values than the operation consumes indexes `STACK[-1]`,\n//!   `STACK[-2]`, ... i.e. before the start of the malloc'd array. Every such\n//!   call in this file is guarded by a `js_gettop()` check.\n//! * `stackidx` (jsrun.c:220) computes `TOP + idx` for `idx < 0`; `idx` values\n//!   near `INT_MIN` overflow that signed addition. The out-of-range probes here\n//!   stay inside +-4200.\n//! * `js_pushlstring(J, v, n)` with `n < 0` (jsrun.c:163) passes the\n//!   `n > JS_STRLIMIT` check and then runs `while (n--) *s++ = *v++`, writing\n//!   ~2^31 bytes past the 16-byte slot.\n//! * `js_isuserdata(J, idx, NULL)` (jsrun.c:266) does `strcmp(tag, ...)` once it\n//!   knows the value is a JS_CUSERDATA, so a NULL tag is only well defined when\n//!   the value at `idx` is *not* userdata. Both cases are exercised, the NULL\n//!   tag only over non-userdata values.\n//! * `js_currentfunctiondata` (jsrun.c:211) reads `STACK[BOT-1].u.object->u.c.data`\n//!   without checking the callee's class. `jsV_newobject` memsets the whole\n//!   object (jsproperty.c:167), so reading `u.c` out of a JS_CFUNCTION is a read\n//!   of zeroed - not uninitialised - memory and is exercised; but there is no\n//!   public way to reach it with BOT-1 holding a JS_CFUNCTION, because native\n//!   code only ever runs with its own JS_CCFUNCTION at BOT-1.\n//! * `js_pushliteral` (jsrun.c:180) stores the caller's pointer, so every\n//!   literal used here has `'static` storage.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::cell::Cell;\nuse std::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void, CString};\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------------- constants */\n\nconst JS_STRLIMIT: c_int = 1 << 28;\nconst JS_STACKSIZE: c_int = 4096;\n\nconst MARK: *const c_char = b\"#\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst LENGTH: *const c_char = b\"length\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst UD_A: *const c_char = b\"UDA\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst UD_B: *const c_char = b\"UDB\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst UD_MISS: *const c_char = b\"NOPE\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst LIT_EMPTY: *const c_char = b\"\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst LIT_1: *const c_char = b\"L\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst LIT_15: *const c_char = b\"L23456789012345\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst LIT_16: *const c_char = b\"L234567890123456\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst LIT_NUM: *const c_char = b\"  12  \\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst S15: *const c_char = b\"S23456789012345\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst S16: *const c_char = b\"S234567890123456\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst RE_PAT: *const c_char = b\"a(b)c\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst PNAME: *const c_char = b\"probe\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst CTOR: *const c_char = b\"Ctor\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst NOOP: *const c_char = b\"noop\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\nconst REG_OP: *const c_char = b\"$op\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst REG_CONV: *const c_char = b\"$conv\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst REG_CMP: *const c_char = b\"$cmp\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst REG_FRAME: *const c_char = b\"$frame\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst REG_TRY: *const c_char = b\"$try\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\nconst REG_CF: *const c_char = b\"$cf\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n\n/// Passed to `js_newuserdata` / `js_newcfunctionx` in BOTH libraries, so the\n/// pointer that comes back out of `js_touserdata` / `js_currentfunctiondata`\n/// can be compared for equality across them.\nstatic mut UD_DATA: [c_int; 4] = [0x5a5a, 0, 0, 0];\n\nfn ud_data() -> *mut c_void {\n    std::ptr::addr_of_mut!(UD_DATA) as *mut c_void\n}\n\n/* --------------------------------------------------------- diff driver */\n\n/// Run `f` against the C library and then the Rust library and assert the two\n/// transcripts (return value plus everything the callbacks pushed into the\n/// per-thread output buffer) are byte-identical.\nfn diff2(tag: &str, f: impl Fn(&Lib) -> String) {\n    let p = libs();\n    let a = {\n        out_clear();\n        set_cur(&p.c);\n        let r = f(&p.c);\n        format!(\"{r}\\n--out--\\n{}\", out_take())\n    };\n    let b = {\n        out_clear();\n        set_cur(&p.rs);\n        let r = f(&p.rs);\n        format!(\"{r}\\n--out--\\n{}\", out_take())\n    };\n    assert_eq!(a, b, \"divergence in [{tag}]\");\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------- slot inspection */\n\n/// Every predicate in rows 57 / 159, in a fixed order, rendered as a bit string.\nconst PREDS: [&str; 17] = [\n    \"js_isdefined\",\n    \"js_isundefined\",\n    \"js_isnull\",\n    \"js_isboolean\",\n    \"js_isnumber\",\n    \"js_isstring\",\n    \"js_isprimitive\",\n    \"js_isobject\",\n    \"js_isarray\",\n    \"js_isregexp\",\n    \"js_iscoercible\",\n    \"js_iscallable\",\n    \"js_iserror\",\n    \"js_isnumberobject\",\n    \"js_isstringobject\",\n    \"js_isbooleanobject\",\n    \"js_isdateobject\",\n];\n\n/// Own/inherited `#` and `length`, read through `js_hasproperty`. Only called\n/// for JS_TOBJECT values (`js_hasproperty` funnels through `js_toobject`, which\n/// throws for undefined/null and *rewrites the slot* for a primitive). None of\n/// the objects built by this file install getters, so `jsR_hasproperty` cannot\n/// re-enter JS and therefore cannot throw.\nunsafe fn objmark(l: &Lib, j: JS, idx: c_int) -> String {\n    let mut s = String::new();\n    for name in [MARK, LENGTH] {\n        if l.js_hasproperty(j, idx, name) != 0 {\n            let n = l.js_tonumber(j, -1);\n            let b = l.js_toboolean(j, -1);\n            l.js_pop(j, 1);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\"{}/{b},\", n));\n        } else {\n            s.push_str(\"-,\");\n        }\n    }\n    s\n}\n\n/// Compact, wholly non-throwing description of one stack slot.\n///\n/// `js_type` / `js_typeof` / the `js_is*` family never throw (jsrun.c:232-283).\n/// `js_tostring` only re-enters JS for JS_TOBJECT (jsvalue.c:330) and\n/// `js_tonumber` / `js_toboolean` likewise, so both are safe once the tag is\n/// known to be primitive.\nunsafe fn slot(l: &Lib, j: JS, idx: c_int) -> String {\n    let t = l.js_type(j, idx);\n    match t {\n        JS_ISUNDEFINED => \"u\".to_string(),\n        JS_ISNULL => \"z\".to_string(),\n        JS_ISBOOLEAN => format!(\"b{}\", l.js_toboolean(j, idx)),\n        JS_ISNUMBER => format!(\"n{:016x}\", l.js_tonumber(j, idx).to_bits()),\n        JS_ISSTRING => format!(\"s{:?}\", from_c(l.js_tostring(j, idx))),\n        _ => format!(\n            \"o{t}:{}:{}{}{}\",\n            from_c(l.js_typeof(j, idx)),\n            objmark(l, j, idx),\n            l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, UD_A),\n            l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, UD_B),\n        ),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Full description: `slot` plus the whole predicate battery.\nunsafe fn vdesc(l: &Lib, j: JS, idx: c_int) -> String {\n    let mut bits = String::new();\n    for name in PREDS {\n        bits.push(if l.pred(name, j, idx) != 0 { '1' } else { '0' });\n    }\n    format!(\"{}|{bits}\", slot(l, j, idx))\n}\n\n/// The whole observable stack: `js_gettop` plus every slot reached through a\n/// positive (BOT-relative) index, every slot reached through a negative\n/// (TOP-relative) index, and a fixed ring of out-of-range indices.\nunsafe fn stack_snap(l: &Lib, j: JS) -> String {\n    let top = l.js_gettop(j);\n    let mut s = format!(\"top={top}\");\n    for i in 0..top {\n        s.push_str(&format!(\" +{i}={}\", slot(l, j, i)));\n    }\n    for i in 1..=top {\n        s.push_str(&format!(\" -{i}={}\", slot(l, j, -i)));\n    }\n    // row 45: out of range in either direction returns the shared static\n    // `undefined` and never faults.\n    for oob in [top, top + 1, top + 37, -(top + 1), -(top + 40), 4100, -4100] {\n        s.push_str(&format!(\" x{oob}={}\", slot(l, j, oob)));\n    }\n    s\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------- value shapes */\n\n/// How to produce one value shape.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\nenum Mk {\n    /// compile+run as a script; its value is left on the stack\n    Js(&'static str),\n    /// one of the native builders in `build_native`\n    Nat(u8),\n    /// `js_pushnumber`\n    Num(f64),\n    /// `js_pushlstring` with `n = bytes.len()` (so embedded NULs survive)\n    Str(Vec<u8>),\n    /// `js_pushliteral` of a NUL-terminated `'static` buffer\n    Lit(&'static [u8]),\n}\n\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_noop(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    l.js_pushnumber(j, 1.0);\n}\n\nunsafe fn build_native(l: &Lib, j: JS, k: u8) {\n    match k {\n        0 => l.js_pushundefined(j),\n        1 => l.js_pushnull(j),\n        2 => l.js_pushboolean(j, 0),\n        3 => l.js_pushboolean(j, 1),\n        // row 58: js_pushboolean takes any int and normalises with !!v\n        4 => l.js_pushboolean(j, 42),\n        5 => l.js_pushboolean(j, -7),\n        6 => l.js_pushboolean(j, c_int::MIN),\n        7 => l.js_pushnumber(j, -0.0),\n        8 => l.js_pushnumber(j, f64::NAN),\n        9 => l.js_pushstring(j, S15),\n        10 => l.js_pushstring(j, S16),\n        // row 67: embedded NUL; all n bytes are stored, consumers stop at NUL\n        11 => l.js_pushlstring(j, b\"a\\0b\".as_ptr() as *const c_char, 3),\n        12 => l.js_pushlstring(j, b\"\\0ab\".as_ptr() as *const c_char, 3),\n        // row 65: n=0 never dereferences v\n        13 => l.js_pushlstring(j, std::ptr::null(), 0),\n        14 => l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_EMPTY),\n        15 => l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_15),\n        16 => l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_16),\n        17 => l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_NUM),\n        // row 70\n        18 => l.js_pushglobal(j),\n        19 => l.js_newobject(j),\n        20 => l.js_newarray(j),\n        21 => l.js_newboolean(j, 0),\n        22 => l.js_newboolean(j, 9),\n        23 => l.js_newnumber(j, -0.0),\n        24 => l.js_newnumber(j, 1.5),\n        25 => l.js_newstring(j, S15),\n        26 => l.js_newstring(j, S16),\n        // row 72: newobjectx with an object on top vs a non-object\n        27 => {\n            l.js_pushglobal(j);\n            l.js_newobjectx(j)\n        }\n        28 => {\n            l.js_pushnumber(j, 3.0);\n            l.js_newobjectx(j)\n        }\n        29 => {\n            l.js_pushnull(j);\n            l.js_newuserdata(j, UD_A, ud_data(), None)\n        }\n        30 => {\n            l.js_pushnull(j);\n            l.js_newuserdata(j, UD_B, std::ptr::null_mut(), None)\n        }\n        31 => l.js_newcfunction(j, Some(cf_noop), NOOP, 3),\n        32 => l.js_newcfunctionx(j, Some(cf_noop), NOOP, 4, ud_data(), None),\n        33 => {\n            l.js_newobject(j);\n            l.js_newcconstructor(j, Some(cf_noop), Some(cf_noop), CTOR, 2)\n        }\n        34 => l.js_newregexp(j, RE_PAT, JS_REGEXP_G | JS_REGEXP_I),\n        35 => l.js_newregexp(j, RE_PAT, 0),\n        _ => panic!(\"bad native shape {k}\"),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Push one shape, leaving exactly one value.\nunsafe fn build_one(l: &Lib, j: JS, m: &Mk) {\n    match m {\n        Mk::Js(src) => {\n            let cs = cstr(src);\n            let rc = l.js_ploadstring(j, FILENAME, cs.as_ptr());\n            assert_eq!(rc, 0, \"{}: shape {src:?} did not compile\", l.name);\n            l.js_pushundefined(j);\n            let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 0);\n            assert_eq!(\n                rc,\n                0,\n                \"{}: shape {src:?} threw {}\",\n                l.name,\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR))\n            );\n        }\n        Mk::Nat(k) => build_native(l, j, *k),\n        Mk::Num(v) => l.js_pushnumber(j, *v),\n        Mk::Str(b) => l.js_pushlstring(j, b.as_ptr() as *const c_char, b.len() as c_int),\n        Mk::Lit(b) => l.js_pushliteral(j, b.as_ptr() as *const c_char),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Build every shape and park it in the registry under `v<i>` so any frame can\n/// re-push the *exact* value (tag included: `jsR_setproperty` stores the\n/// `js_Value` verbatim, jsrun.c:971).\nunsafe fn build_shapes(l: &Lib, j: JS, list: &[Mk]) -> Vec<CString> {\n    let mut names = Vec::with_capacity(list.len());\n    for (i, m) in list.iter().enumerate() {\n        let base = l.js_gettop(j);\n        build_one(l, j, m);\n        assert_eq!(\n            l.js_gettop(j),\n            base + 1,\n            \"{}: shape {i} {m:?} pushed {} values\",\n            l.name,\n            l.js_gettop(j) - base\n        );\n        let n = CString::new(format!(\"v{i}\")).unwrap();\n        l.js_setregistry(j, n.as_ptr());\n        names.push(n);\n    }\n    names\n}\n\n/// The full shape list: every value tag, every object class, both string\n/// storage classes, and the throwing conversions.\nfn shapes_full() -> Vec<Mk> {\n    let mut v: Vec<Mk> = vec![];\n    for s in [\n        \"undefined\", \"null\", \"true\", \"false\", \"0\", \"-0\", \"NaN\", \"Infinity\",\n        \"-Infinity\", \"1\", \"-1\", \"0.5\", \"-3.25\", \"1e21\", \"1e-7\", \"1e300\", \"5e-324\",\n        \"2147483647\", \"-2147483648\", \"4294967296\", \"65536\", \"65535\", \"32768\",\n        \"1/3\", \"''\", \"'a'\", \"'abc'\", \"'0'\", \"'1'\", \"'  12  '\", \"'0x1f'\",\n        \"'Infinity'\", \"'-Infinity'\", \"'12abc'\", \"'1.5'\", \"'1e3'\",\n        \"'0123456789abcde'\", \"'0123456789abcdef'\", \"'true'\", \"({})\",\n        \"({a:1,b:'x'})\", \"[]\", \"[1,2,3]\",\n        \"(function(){var a=[1,2];a[5]=6;return a})()\",\n        \"(function f(a,b){return a})\", \"print\", \"Math\", \"JSON\", \"/a(b)c/gi\",\n        \"new Date(0)\", \"new Date(1234567890)\", \"new Number(5)\", \"new Number(0)\",\n        \"new String('xy')\", \"new String('')\", \"new Boolean(false)\",\n        \"new Boolean(true)\", \"new Error('boom')\", \"new TypeError('bad')\",\n        \"Object.create(null)\", \"({toString:function(){throw 'TS!'}})\",\n        \"({valueOf:function(){throw 'VO!'}})\", \"({valueOf:function(){return 7}})\",\n        \"({toString:function(){return 'TS'}})\",\n        \"({valueOf:function(){return {}},toString:function(){return {}}})\",\n        \"Object.prototype\", \"Array.prototype\", \"Function.prototype\",\n    ] {\n        v.push(Mk::Js(s));\n    }\n    for k in 0..=35u8 {\n        v.push(Mk::Nat(k));\n    }\n    // randomised doubles and strings (fixed seed)\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x5741_0C_5ACK);\n    for _ in 0..24 {\n        v.push(Mk::Num(rng.f64_sane()));\n    }\n    for _ in 0..8 {\n        v.push(Mk::Num(rng.f64_any()));\n    }\n    for _ in 0..10 {\n        v.push(Mk::Str(rng.ascii_string(24).into_bytes()));\n    }\n    for _ in 0..8 {\n        v.push(Mk::Str(rng.unicode_string(8).into_bytes()));\n    }\n    for _ in 0..8 {\n        v.push(Mk::Str(rng.raw_bytes(20)));\n    }\n    v.push(Mk::Lit(b\"lit\\0\"));\n    v.push(Mk::Lit(b\"0\\0\"));\n    v\n}\n\n/// A curated ~46-element subset for the O(n^2) comparison cross product.\nfn shapes_cross() -> Vec<Mk> {\n    let mut v: Vec<Mk> = vec![];\n    for s in [\n        \"undefined\", \"null\", \"true\", \"false\", \"0\", \"-0\", \"NaN\", \"Infinity\",\n        \"-Infinity\", \"1\", \"-1\", \"0.5\", \"1e21\", \"2147483647\", \"''\", \"'a'\", \"'0'\",\n        \"'1'\", \"'  12  '\", \"'0x1f'\", \"'Infinity'\", \"'12abc'\",\n        \"'0123456789abcdef'\", \"({})\", \"({a:1})\", \"[]\", \"[1,2,3]\", \"[1]\",\n        \"(function f(a,b){return a})\", \"print\", \"Math\", \"/a(b)c/gi\",\n        \"new Date(0)\", \"new Number(5)\", \"new String('xy')\", \"new String('1')\",\n        \"new Boolean(false)\", \"new Error('boom')\", \"Object.create(null)\",\n        \"({toString:function(){throw 'TS!'}})\", \"({valueOf:function(){return 7}})\",\n        \"Object\", \"Array\",\n    ] {\n        v.push(Mk::Js(s));\n    }\n    v.push(Mk::Nat(4)); // js_pushboolean(42)\n    v.push(Mk::Nat(11)); // \"a\\0b\"\n    v.push(Mk::Nat(15)); // literal, 15 bytes\n    v.push(Mk::Nat(29)); // userdata\n    v.push(Mk::Num(-0.0));\n    v.push(Mk::Lit(b\"1\\0\"));\n    v\n}\n\n/* ----------------------------------------------------- probe machinery */\n\nthread_local! {\n    static OP: Cell<u32> = const { Cell::new(0) };\n    static A0: Cell<c_int> = const { Cell::new(0) };\n    static NPRE: Cell<c_int> = const { Cell::new(0) };\n    static NAME_A: Cell<*const c_char> = const { Cell::new(std::ptr::null()) };\n    static NAME_B: Cell<*const c_char> = const { Cell::new(std::ptr::null()) };\n    static OKAY: Cell<c_int> = const { Cell::new(-1) };\n    static DEPTH: Cell<c_int> = const { Cell::new(0) };\n}\n\nunsafe fn install(l: &Lib, j: JS, f: js_CFunction, reg: *const c_char) {\n    l.js_newcfunction(j, f, PNAME, 0);\n    l.js_setregistry(j, reg);\n}\n\n/// Call a registry-parked cfunction through `js_pcall`, then report the return\n/// code, the (repr of the) result and that the frame was balanced.\nunsafe fn run(l: &Lib, j: JS, reg: *const c_char) -> String {\n    let base = l.js_gettop(j);\n    l.js_getregistry(j, reg);\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n    let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 0);\n    let res = from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR));\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    let after = l.js_gettop(j);\n    format!(\"rc={rc} res={res:?} top={after}(was {base})\")\n}\n\n/* ============================================================ rows 41-54 */\n\n/// One randomised stack-operation sequence. Op codes:\n/// pushes 0-9, `js_pop` 10, `js_copy` 11, `js_remove` 12, `js_replace` 13,\n/// `js_dup` 14, `js_dup2` 15, `js_rot2` 16, `js_rot3` 17, `js_rot4` 18,\n/// `js_rot2pop1` 19, `js_rot3pop2` 20, `js_rot` 21.\nunsafe fn seq(l: &Lib, seed: u64) -> String {\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(seed);\n    let j = new_state(l, 0);\n    let mut t = String::new();\n    let mut uniq = 0i64;\n    let mut next = |r: &mut Rng, u: &mut i64| -> f64 {\n        *u += 1;\n        *u as f64 + (r.below(4) as f64) / 8.0\n    };\n\n    // a marked global so the JS_TOBJECT slots stay distinguishable\n    l.js_pushglobal(j);\n    l.js_pushnumber(j, -1.0);\n    l.js_setproperty(j, -2, MARK);\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n\n    let nstart = rng.below(6) as c_int;\n    for _ in 0..nstart {\n        let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n        l.js_pushnumber(j, v);\n    }\n    let nops = 20 + rng.below(61);\n    t.push_str(&format!(\"start {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)));\n    for step in 0..nops {\n        let top = l.js_gettop(j);\n        let mut op = rng.below(22);\n        // keep the frame bounded so CHECKSTACK never fires here (row 55 has its\n        // own test) and so pushes stay interesting\n        if top >= 32 && op < 10 {\n            op = 10 + rng.below(12);\n        }\n        if top < 8 && op >= 10 {\n            op = rng.below(10);\n        }\n        let desc: String = match op {\n            0 => {\n                l.js_pushundefined(j);\n                \"pushundefined\".into()\n            }\n            1 => {\n                l.js_pushnull(j);\n                \"pushnull\".into()\n            }\n            2 => {\n                let b = [0, 1, 42, -3, c_int::MIN][rng.below(5) as usize];\n                l.js_pushboolean(j, b);\n                format!(\"pushboolean({b})\")\n            }\n            3 => {\n                let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, v);\n                format!(\"pushnumber({v})\")\n            }\n            4 => {\n                let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n                let s = cstr(&format!(\"s{v}\"));\n                l.js_pushstring(j, s.as_ptr());\n                format!(\"pushstring(s{v})\")\n            }\n            5 => {\n                let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n                let s = cstr(&format!(\"mem-{v}-0123456789abcdef\"));\n                l.js_pushstring(j, s.as_ptr());\n                format!(\"pushstring(long {v})\")\n            }\n            6 => {\n                let k = rng.below(4);\n                let p = [LIT_EMPTY, LIT_1, LIT_15, LIT_16][k as usize];\n                l.js_pushliteral(j, p);\n                format!(\"pushliteral({k})\")\n            }\n            7 => {\n                l.js_pushglobal(j);\n                \"pushglobal\".into()\n            }\n            8 => {\n                let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n                l.js_newobject(j);\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, v);\n                l.js_setproperty(j, -2, MARK);\n                format!(\"newobject({v})\")\n            }\n            9 => {\n                let v = next(&mut rng, &mut uniq);\n                l.js_newarray(j);\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, v);\n                l.js_setproperty(j, -2, MARK);\n                format!(\"newarray({v})\")\n            }\n            // rows 42/43: n=0 and n == js_gettop are the two non-throwing ends\n            10 => {\n                let n = rng.below(top as u32 + 1) as c_int;\n                l.js_pop(j, n);\n                format!(\"pop({n})\")\n            }\n            // rows 44/45: any index, in range or not, is well defined\n            11 => {\n                let idx = pick_idx(&mut rng, top);\n                l.js_copy(j, idx);\n                format!(\"copy({idx})\")\n            }\n            12 => {\n                let idx = pick_valid(&mut rng, top);\n                l.js_remove(j, idx);\n                format!(\"remove({idx})\")\n            }\n            13 => {\n                let idx = pick_valid(&mut rng, top);\n                l.js_replace(j, idx);\n                format!(\"replace({idx})\")\n            }\n            14 => {\n                l.nullary(\"js_dup\", j);\n                \"dup\".into()\n            }\n            15 => {\n                if top < 2 {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_dup\", j);\n                    \"dup(dup2 needs 2)\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_dup2\", j);\n                    \"dup2\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            16 => {\n                if top < 2 {\n                    \"skip rot2\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_rot2\", j);\n                    \"rot2\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            17 => {\n                if top < 3 {\n                    \"skip rot3\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_rot3\", j);\n                    \"rot3\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            18 => {\n                if top < 4 {\n                    \"skip rot4\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_rot4\", j);\n                    \"rot4\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            19 => {\n                if top < 2 {\n                    \"skip rot2pop1\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_rot2pop1\", j);\n                    \"rot2pop1\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            20 => {\n                if top < 3 {\n                    \"skip rot3pop2\".into()\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_rot3pop2\", j);\n                    \"rot3pop2\".into()\n                }\n            }\n            _ => {\n                // row 54: n<=1 is a no-op, n=2 is js_rot2, n=k>2 rotates k.\n                // n > js_gettop() would index below the array (see the file\n                // header), so it is clamped here.\n                let n = rng.below(top as u32 + 1) as c_int;\n                l.js_rot(j, n);\n                format!(\"rot({n})\")\n            }\n        };\n        t.push_str(&format!(\"{step} {desc} -> {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)));\n    }\n    l.js_freestate(j);\n    t\n}\n\n/// Any index at all: `stackidx` is total for BOT == 0.\nfn pick_idx(rng: &mut Rng, top: c_int) -> c_int {\n    match rng.below(6) {\n        0 => rng.range(0, top.max(1) as i64) as c_int,\n        1 => -(1 + rng.range(0, top.max(1) as i64) as c_int),\n        2 => top + rng.below(4) as c_int,\n        3 => -(top + 1 + rng.below(4) as c_int),\n        4 => rng.range(-4100, 4100) as c_int,\n        _ => 0,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Only the indices `js_remove` / `js_replace` accept without raising\n/// js_error \"stack error!\" (jsrun.c:412 / :427).\nfn pick_valid(rng: &mut Rng, top: c_int) -> c_int {\n    assert!(top >= 1);\n    if rng.below(2) == 0 {\n        rng.range(0, top as i64) as c_int\n    } else {\n        -(1 + rng.range(0, top as i64) as c_int)\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rows 41-54: randomised operation sequences with the whole observable stack\n/// compared after every single step.\n#[test]\nfn t_stack_ops_random() {\n    for s in 0..28u64 {\n        let seed = 0x5732_0000 + s * 7919;\n        diff2(&format!(\"seq seed={seed}\"), move |l| unsafe { seq(l, seed) });\n    }\n}\n\n/* =================================================== rows 43/47/49/50/55 */\n\n/// The op driver used for everything that can throw. `NPRE` values are pushed\n/// first so the frame shape is known, then op `OP` runs with argument `A0`.\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_op(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    let npre = NPRE.with(|c| c.get());\n    for i in 0..npre {\n        l.js_pushnumber(j, 100.0 + i as f64);\n    }\n    out_push(format!(\"  pre {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)).as_bytes());\n    let op = OP.with(|c| c.get());\n    let a0 = A0.with(|c| c.get());\n    match op {\n        0 => l.js_pop(j, a0),\n        1 => l.js_remove(j, a0),\n        2 => l.js_replace(j, a0),\n        3 => l.js_insert(j, a0),\n        4 => l.js_rot(j, a0),\n        5 => l.js_copy(j, a0),\n        6 => l.js_pushlstring(j, std::ptr::null(), 0),\n        7 => l.js_pushlstring(j, S16, a0),\n        8 => l.js_pushstring(j, S16),\n        9 => {\n            // row 55: push until CHECKSTACK fires\n            for i in 0..(JS_STACKSIZE + 64) {\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, i as f64);\n            }\n        }\n        10 => {\n            // row 55 through js_copy / js_dup / js_dup2\n            for i in 0..(JS_STACKSIZE + 64) {\n                if i % 3 == 0 {\n                    l.js_copy(j, 0);\n                } else if i % 3 == 1 {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_dup\", j);\n                } else {\n                    l.nullary(\"js_dup2\", j);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        11 => l.js_currentfunction(j),\n        _ => {}\n    }\n    if op == 9 || op == 10 {\n        out_push(format!(\"  post top={}\\n\", l.js_gettop(j)).as_bytes());\n    } else {\n        out_push(format!(\"  post {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)).as_bytes());\n    }\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n}\n\n/// Rows 43 / 47 / 49 / 50: every throwing stack operation, always inside a\n/// protected `js_pcall` frame (so BOT > 0 and the \"below BOT\" arm of the\n/// `idx < BOT` check in jsrun.c:415 / :430 is reachable).\n#[test]\nfn t_stack_errors() {\n    for npre in [0i32, 1, 3] {\n        for (op, name) in [\n            (0u32, \"pop\"),\n            (1, \"remove\"),\n            (2, \"replace\"),\n            (3, \"insert\"),\n            (5, \"copy\"),\n        ] {\n            for a0 in [\n                -9999i32, -100, -(npre + 6), -(npre + 2), -(npre + 1), -npre - 1, -3, -2,\n                -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, npre, npre + 1, npre + 2, npre + 40, 4099, 100000,\n            ] {\n                let tag = format!(\"{name}({a0}) npre={npre}\");\n                diff2(&tag, move |l| unsafe {\n                    let j = new_state(l, 0);\n                    install(l, j, Some(cf_op), REG_OP);\n                    l.js_pushnumber(j, 7.0);\n                    l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_15);\n                    OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n                    A0.with(|c| c.set(a0));\n                    NPRE.with(|c| c.set(npre));\n                    let r = run(l, j, REG_OP);\n                    let after = stack_snap(l, j);\n                    l.js_freestate(j);\n                    format!(\"{r}\\nafter {after}\")\n                });\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Row 50: `js_insert` is unconditionally `js_error(J, \"not implemented yet\")`\n/// (jsrun.c:422-425), whatever the index and whatever the stack looks like.\n#[test]\nfn t_insert_never_implemented() {\n    for npre in [0i32, 1, 2, 5] {\n        for a0 in [c_int::MIN + 1, -4096, -7, -1, 0, 1, 5, 4096, c_int::MAX - 1] {\n            let tag = format!(\"insert({a0}) npre={npre}\");\n            diff2(&tag, move |l| unsafe {\n                let j = new_state(l, 0);\n                install(l, j, Some(cf_op), REG_OP);\n                OP.with(|c| c.set(3));\n                A0.with(|c| c.set(a0));\n                NPRE.with(|c| c.set(npre));\n                let r = run(l, j, REG_OP);\n                l.js_freestate(j);\n                r\n            });\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rows 55 / 64 / 65: CHECKSTACK overflow, the JS_STRLIMIT guard (which fires\n/// before any copying, so a 16-byte buffer with a huge `n` is safe), and\n/// `js_pushlstring(v, 0)` with a NULL pointer.\n#[test]\nfn t_push_limits() {\n    for (op, a0, tag) in [\n        (6u32, 0i32, \"pushlstring(NULL,0)\"),\n        (7, JS_STRLIMIT + 1, \"pushlstring(n=STRLIMIT+1)\"),\n        (7, JS_STRLIMIT + 4096, \"pushlstring(n=STRLIMIT+4096)\"),\n        (7, c_int::MAX, \"pushlstring(n=INT_MAX)\"),\n        (7, 0, \"pushlstring(n=0)\"),\n        (7, 15, \"pushlstring(n=15)\"),\n        (7, 16, \"pushlstring(n=16)\"),\n        (8, 0, \"pushstring(16)\"),\n        (9, 0, \"overflow via pushnumber\"),\n        (10, 0, \"overflow via copy/dup/dup2\"),\n        (11, 0, \"currentfunction in frame\"),\n    ] {\n        diff2(tag, move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, 0);\n            install(l, j, Some(cf_op), REG_OP);\n            OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n            A0.with(|c| c.set(a0));\n            NPRE.with(|c| c.set(2));\n            let r = run(l, j, REG_OP);\n            let after = stack_snap(l, j);\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            format!(\"{r}\\nafter {after}\")\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n/* ================================================== rows 41/44/56: frames */\n\n/// Reports its frame, duplicates `this` with `js_copy(J, 0)` (row 44), asks for\n/// `js_currentfunction` / `js_currentfunctiondata` (row 56) and then recurses so\n/// that BOT keeps growing.\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_frame(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    let top = l.js_gettop(j);\n    let mut s = format!(\"  frame gettop={top}\");\n    for i in 0..top {\n        s.push_str(&format!(\" a{i}={}\", slot(l, j, i)));\n    }\n    l.js_copy(j, 0);\n    s.push_str(&format!(\" this={} top={}\", slot(l, j, -1), l.js_gettop(j)));\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    l.js_currentfunction(j);\n    s.push_str(&format!(\n        \" curfn={} top={}\",\n        slot(l, j, -1),\n        l.js_gettop(j)\n    ));\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    let d = l.js_currentfunctiondata(j);\n    s.push_str(&format!(\n        \" curdata={}\",\n        if d.is_null() {\n            \"NULL\".to_string()\n        } else if d == ud_data() {\n            \"UD_DATA\".to_string()\n        } else {\n            \"other\".to_string()\n        }\n    ));\n    s.push('\\n');\n    out_push(s.as_bytes());\n\n    let d = DEPTH.with(|c| c.get());\n    if d > 0 {\n        DEPTH.with(|c| c.set(d - 1));\n        l.js_getregistry(j, REG_FRAME);\n        l.js_pushnumber(j, 7.0 + d as f64);\n        l.js_pushnumber(j, d as f64);\n        l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_15);\n        let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 2);\n        out_push(format!(\"  nested rc={rc} res={}\\n\", slot(l, j, -1)).as_bytes());\n        l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    }\n    l.js_pushnumber(j, 42.0 + top as f64);\n}\n\n/// Rows 41 / 44 / 56: `js_gettop` at top level (BOT==0) vs inside nested\n/// cfunction frames, `js_copy(J, 0)` reaching `this`, and\n/// `js_currentfunction` / `js_currentfunctiondata` in both places.\n#[test]\nfn t_frames_and_currentfunction() {\n    for depth in [0i32, 1, 3] {\n        for data in [false, true] {\n            let tag = format!(\"frame depth={depth} data={data}\");\n            diff2(&tag, move |l| unsafe {\n                let j = new_state(l, 0);\n                if data {\n                    l.js_newcfunctionx(j, Some(cf_frame), PNAME, 0, ud_data(), None);\n                } else {\n                    l.js_newcfunction(j, Some(cf_frame), PNAME, 0);\n                }\n                l.js_setregistry(j, REG_FRAME);\n\n                // row 56 at BOT == 0\n                l.js_currentfunction(j);\n                let mut s = format!(\"toplevel curfn={} \", slot(l, j, -1));\n                l.js_pop(j, 1);\n                let d = l.js_currentfunctiondata(j);\n                s.push_str(&format!(\"curdata_null={} \", d.is_null()));\n                s.push_str(&format!(\"gettop={}\\n\", l.js_gettop(j)));\n\n                DEPTH.with(|c| c.set(depth));\n                l.js_getregistry(j, REG_FRAME);\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, 1.0);\n                let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 0);\n                s.push_str(&format!(\n                    \"rc={rc} res={} top={}\\n\",\n                    slot(l, j, -1),\n                    l.js_gettop(j)\n                ));\n                l.js_pop(j, 1);\n\n                // and with arguments, so BOT-relative indices 1..n are populated\n                DEPTH.with(|c| c.set(depth));\n                l.js_getregistry(j, REG_FRAME);\n                l.js_pushnull(j);\n                l.js_pushnumber(j, 2.5);\n                l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_16);\n                l.js_pushglobal(j);\n                let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 3);\n                s.push_str(&format!(\n                    \"rc={rc} res={} top={}\\n\",\n                    slot(l, j, -1),\n                    l.js_gettop(j)\n                ));\n                l.js_pop(j, 1);\n                s.push_str(&format!(\"end {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)));\n                l.js_freestate(j);\n                s\n            });\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/* =========================================== rows 57-70: pushes + strings */\n\n/// Distinguish JS_TSHRSTR / JS_TLITSTR / JS_TMEMSTR without reading the tag.\n///\n/// `jsV_tostring` (jsvalue.c:330) hands back `v->u.shrstr` for JS_TSHRSTR, i.e.\n/// a pointer INTO the 16-byte stack slot; for JS_TLITSTR it hands back the\n/// caller's own pointer and for JS_TMEMSTR the `js_String` payload. So copying\n/// the value to a fresh slot changes the pointer only for a SHRSTR, and\n/// comparing against the literal we pushed separates LITSTR from MEMSTR.\nunsafe fn strtag(l: &Lib, j: JS, idx: c_int, lit: *const c_char) -> &'static str {\n    if l.pred(\"js_isstring\", j, idx) == 0 {\n        return \"-\";\n    }\n    let p1 = l.js_tostring(j, idx);\n    l.js_copy(j, idx);\n    let p2 = l.js_tostring(j, -1);\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    if p1 != p2 {\n        \"SHRSTR\"\n    } else if !lit.is_null() && p1 == lit {\n        \"LITSTR\"\n    } else {\n        \"MEMSTR\"\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rows 57-70: every push entry point over the SHRSTR / LITSTR / MEMSTR length\n/// axis (the threshold is `n <= soffsetof(js_Value, t.type)` == 15 in\n/// jsrun.c:145/163, and `n < sizeof(obj->u.s.shrstr)` == 16 in jsvalue.c:385 --\n/// `<=15` vs `<16`, the same set of lengths reached through different\n/// spellings), including empty strings, embedded NULs and non-0/1 booleans.\n#[test]\nfn t_pushes_and_strings() {\n    // string bodies straddling both thresholds\n    let mut bodies: Vec<Vec<u8>> = vec![];\n    for n in 0..=20usize {\n        bodies.push((0..n).map(|i| b'a' + (i % 26) as u8).collect());\n    }\n    for n in [30usize, 31, 32, 63, 64, 65] {\n        bodies.push((0..n).map(|i| b'A' + (i % 26) as u8).collect());\n    }\n    bodies.push(b\"a\\0b\".to_vec());\n    bodies.push(b\"\\0abc\".to_vec());\n    bodies.push(b\"abcdefghijklmno\\0extra\".to_vec());\n    bodies.push(b\"0123456789abcde\\0\".to_vec());\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0x9E37_79B9);\n    for _ in 0..40 {\n        bodies.push(rng.ascii_string(20).into_bytes());\n    }\n    for _ in 0..20 {\n        bodies.push(rng.unicode_string(8).into_bytes());\n    }\n    for _ in 0..20 {\n        bodies.push(rng.raw_bytes(20));\n    }\n\n    for body in &bodies {\n        let body = body.clone();\n        let tag = format!(\"push {body:?}\");\n        diff2(&tag, move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, 0);\n            let mut s = String::new();\n            // NUL-terminated copy for the strlen-based entry points\n            let mut z = body.clone();\n            z.push(0);\n            let zp = z.as_ptr() as *const c_char;\n            for (k, what) in [\n                (0u32, \"pushstring\"),\n                (1, \"pushlstring(len)\"),\n                (2, \"pushliteral\"),\n                (3, \"newstring\"),\n                (4, \"pushlstring(half)\"),\n            ] {\n                let base = l.js_gettop(j);\n                match k {\n                    0 => l.js_pushstring(j, zp),\n                    1 => l.js_pushlstring(j, body.as_ptr() as *const c_char, body.len() as c_int),\n                    2 => l.js_pushliteral(j, zp),\n                    3 => l.js_newstring(j, zp),\n                    _ => l.js_pushlstring(\n                        j,\n                        body.as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n                        (body.len() / 2) as c_int,\n                    ),\n                }\n                let lit = if k == 2 { zp } else { std::ptr::null() };\n                s.push_str(&format!(\n                    \"{what}: top={} tag={} v={} repr={:?} bool={} num={:016x}\\n\",\n                    l.js_gettop(j) - base,\n                    strtag(l, j, -1, lit),\n                    vdesc(l, j, -1),\n                    from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR)),\n                    l.js_tryboolean(j, -1, 9),\n                    l.js_trynumber(j, -1, -1.0).to_bits(),\n                ));\n                l.js_pop(j, l.js_gettop(j) - base);\n            }\n            // row 69: the same bytes as LITSTR and as SHRSTR/MEMSTR still\n            // compare equal, because both comparisons are strcmp-based\n            l.js_pushliteral(j, zp);\n            l.js_pushstring(j, zp);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"lit-vs-str equal={} strict={} cmp={}\\n\",\n                l.nullary_i(\"js_equal\", j),\n                l.nullary_i(\"js_strictequal\", j),\n                {\n                    let ok = OKAY.with(|c| c.as_ptr());\n                    let r = l.js_compare(j, ok);\n                    format!(\"{r}/{}\", OKAY.with(|c| c.get()))\n                }\n            ));\n            l.js_pop(j, 2);\n            // row 62: the SHRSTR/MEMSTR split is visible in the GC's string count\n            l.js_pushstring(j, zp);\n            l.js_pushlstring(j, body.as_ptr() as *const c_char, body.len() as c_int);\n            out_clear();\n            l.js_gc(j, 1);\n            let gc = out_take();\n            l.js_pop(j, 2);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\"gc {gc}\"));\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            s\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rows 57-60 / 70-73: the non-string pushes and constructors, plus the exact\n/// stack effect of each.\n#[test]\nfn t_push_values_and_new() {\n    let mut nums: Vec<f64> = vec![\n        0.0, -0.0, 1.0, -1.0, 0.5, -3.25, f64::NAN, f64::INFINITY,\n        f64::NEG_INFINITY, 1e21, 1e-7, 1e300, 5e-324, 2147483647.0, -2147483648.0,\n        2147483648.0, 4294967295.0, 4294967296.0, 65535.0, 65536.0, 32768.0,\n        1.0 / 3.0, 1.2345678901234567e300, 1e-323,\n    ];\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xDEAD_BEEF);\n    for _ in 0..120 {\n        nums.push(rng.f64_sane());\n    }\n    for _ in 0..60 {\n        nums.push(rng.f64_any());\n    }\n    diff2(\"push numbers\", move |l| unsafe {\n        let j = new_state(l, 0);\n        let mut s = String::new();\n        for v in &nums {\n            l.js_pushnumber(j, *v);\n            l.js_newnumber(j, *v);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"{:016x}: prim={} repr={:?} str={:?} obj={} orepr={:?}\\n\",\n                v.to_bits(),\n                vdesc(l, j, -2),\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -2, ERRSTR)),\n                from_c(l.js_trystring(j, -2, ERRSTR)),\n                vdesc(l, j, -1),\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR)),\n            ));\n            l.js_pop(j, 2);\n        }\n        l.js_freestate(j);\n        s\n    });\n\n    diff2(\"push misc\", |l| unsafe {\n        let j = new_state(l, 0);\n        let mut s = String::new();\n        for k in 0..=35u8 {\n            let base = l.js_gettop(j);\n            build_native(l, j, k);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"nat{k}: pushed={} {} repr={:?} str={:?} tag={}\\n\",\n                l.js_gettop(j) - base,\n                vdesc(l, j, -1),\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR)),\n                from_c(l.js_trystring(j, -1, ERRSTR)),\n                strtag(l, j, -1, std::ptr::null()),\n            ));\n        }\n        s.push_str(&format!(\"all {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)));\n        l.js_freestate(j);\n        s\n    });\n\n    // rows 57/58 in isolation, over the whole int range of js_pushboolean\n    diff2(\"pushboolean ints\", |l| unsafe {\n        let j = new_state(l, 0);\n        let mut s = String::new();\n        let mut rng = Rng::new(0x00B0_01);\n        let mut vals: Vec<c_int> = vec![0, 1, -1, 2, 42, c_int::MIN, c_int::MAX, 256, 0x100];\n        for _ in 0..64 {\n            vals.push(rng.next_u32() as c_int);\n        }\n        for v in vals {\n            l.js_pushboolean(j, v);\n            l.js_pushboolean(j, 1);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"{v}: {} strict1={} eq1={} repr={:?}\\n\",\n                vdesc(l, j, -2),\n                l.nullary_i(\"js_strictequal\", j),\n                l.nullary_i(\"js_equal\", j),\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -2, ERRSTR)),\n            ));\n            l.js_pop(j, 2);\n        }\n        l.js_freestate(j);\n        s\n    });\n}\n\n/* ============================================ rows 142-158/160/161/164/168 */\n\n/// One conversion applied to one registry-parked shape, with the stack slot\n/// described before and after (rows 150/151: `js_tostring` on a JS_TNUMBER and\n/// `js_toobject` on a primitive rewrite the slot in place).\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_conv(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    l.js_getregistry(j, NAME_A.with(|c| c.get()));\n    out_push(format!(\"  pre={}\\n\", vdesc(l, j, -1)).as_bytes());\n    let op = OP.with(|c| c.get());\n    let r: String = match op {\n        0 => format!(\"toboolean={}\", l.js_toboolean(j, -1)),\n        1 => format!(\"tonumber={:016x}\", l.js_tonumber(j, -1).to_bits()),\n        2 => format!(\"tostring={:?}\", from_c(l.js_tostring(j, -1))),\n        3 => format!(\"tointeger={}\", l.js_tointeger(j, -1)),\n        4 => format!(\"toint32={}\", l.js_toint32(j, -1)),\n        5 => format!(\"touint32={}\", l.js_touint32(j, -1)),\n        6 => format!(\"toint16={}\", l.js_toint16(j, -1)),\n        7 => format!(\"touint16={}\", l.js_touint16(j, -1)),\n        8 => format!(\"typeof={}\", from_c(l.js_typeof(j, -1))),\n        9 => format!(\"type={}\", l.js_type(j, -1)),\n        10 => {\n            l.js_repr(j, -1);\n            format!(\n                \"repr={:?} pushed_top={} under={}\",\n                from_c(l.js_tostring(j, -1)),\n                l.js_gettop(j),\n                vdesc(l, j, -2)\n            )\n        }\n        11 => format!(\"torepr={:?}\", from_c(l.js_torepr(j, -1))),\n        12 => format!(\"trystring={:?}\", from_c(l.js_trystring(j, -1, ERRSTR))),\n        13 => format!(\"trynumber={:016x}\", l.js_trynumber(j, -1, -12345.5).to_bits()),\n        14 => format!(\"tryinteger={}\", l.js_tryinteger(j, -1, -777)),\n        15 => format!(\"tryboolean={}\", l.js_tryboolean(j, -1, 7)),\n        16 => format!(\"tryrepr={:?}\", from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR))),\n        17 => {\n            let f = l.raw2::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(JS, c_int) -> *mut c_void>(\"js_toobject\");\n            let o = f(j, -1);\n            format!(\"toobject_null={}\", o.is_null())\n        }\n        18 => {\n            let f = l.raw2::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(JS, c_int, c_int)>(\"js_toprimitive\");\n            f(j, -1, A0.with(|c| c.get()));\n            \"toprimitive\".to_string()\n        }\n        19 => {\n            let f =\n                l.raw2::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(JS, c_int, *const c_char) -> *mut c_void>(\n                    \"js_touserdata\",\n                );\n            let p = f(j, -1, if A0.with(|c| c.get()) == 0 { UD_A } else { UD_MISS });\n            format!(\n                \"touserdata={}\",\n                if p.is_null() {\n                    \"NULL\"\n                } else if p == ud_data() {\n                    \"UD_DATA\"\n                } else {\n                    \"other\"\n                }\n            )\n        }\n        20 => {\n            let f = l.raw2::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(JS, c_int) -> *mut c_void>(\"js_toregexp\");\n            let p = f(j, -1);\n            format!(\"toregexp_null={}\", p.is_null())\n        }\n        _ => \"?\".to_string(),\n    };\n    out_push(format!(\"  {r}\\n  post={} top={}\\n\", vdesc(l, j, -1), l.js_gettop(j)).as_bytes());\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n}\n\n/// Rows 142-158, 160, 161, 163, 164, 168: every conversion over every value\n/// shape, in both strict and non-strict states (row 149 depends on\n/// `J->strict`).\n#[test]\nfn t_conversions() {\n    let list = shapes_full();\n    for flags in [0, JS_STRICT] {\n        let list = list.clone();\n        diff2(&format!(\"conversions flags={flags}\"), move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, flags);\n            let names = build_shapes(l, j, &list);\n            install(l, j, Some(cf_conv), REG_CONV);\n            let mut s = String::new();\n            for (i, n) in names.iter().enumerate() {\n                NAME_A.with(|c| c.set(n.as_ptr()));\n                for op in 0..=17u32 {\n                    OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n                    out_push(format!(\"shape{i} op{op}\\n\").as_bytes());\n                    s.push_str(&format!(\"s{i}o{op} {}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_CONV)));\n                }\n                // js_toprimitive over all three hints\n                OP.with(|c| c.set(18));\n                for hint in 0..3 {\n                    A0.with(|c| c.set(hint));\n                    out_push(format!(\"shape{i} toprim{hint}\\n\").as_bytes());\n                    s.push_str(&format!(\"s{i}p{hint} {}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_CONV)));\n                }\n                // row 163: js_touserdata with the right tag and a wrong one,\n                // and js_toregexp\n                for (op, a0) in [(19u32, 0), (19, 1), (20, 0)] {\n                    OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n                    A0.with(|c| c.set(a0));\n                    out_push(format!(\"shape{i} op{op}/{a0}\\n\").as_bytes());\n                    s.push_str(&format!(\"s{i}u{op}_{a0} {}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_CONV)));\n                }\n            }\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            s\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n/* ================================================= row 162: the try limit */\n\n/// Recurses through `js_pcall` (one `js_try` per level) until `trytop` reaches\n/// JS_TRYLIMIT, then calls the four `js_ptry`-guarded conversions.\n///\n/// `js_tryrepr` (jsrepr.c:275) has NO `js_ptry` pre-check, so at the limit its\n/// `js_savetry` throws into the enclosing frame instead of returning the\n/// default; that case is covered by tests/api_state.rs and is deliberately not\n/// repeated here.\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_try(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    let d = DEPTH.with(|c| c.get());\n    if d > 0 {\n        DEPTH.with(|c| c.set(d - 1));\n        l.js_getregistry(j, REG_TRY);\n        l.js_pushundefined(j);\n        let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 0);\n        if rc != 0 {\n            out_push(format!(\"  depth{d} rc={rc}\\n\").as_bytes());\n        }\n        l.js_pop(j, 1);\n        l.js_pushundefined(j);\n        return;\n    }\n    l.js_getregistry(j, NAME_A.with(|c| c.get()));\n    out_push(\n        format!(\n            \"  limit: str={:?} num={:016x} int={} bool={} top={}\\n\",\n            from_c(l.js_trystring(j, -1, ERRSTR)),\n            l.js_trynumber(j, -1, -12345.5).to_bits(),\n            l.js_tryinteger(j, -1, -777),\n            l.js_tryboolean(j, -1, 7),\n            l.js_gettop(j)\n        )\n        .as_bytes(),\n    );\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n}\n\n/// Rows 160-162: the try* conversions on a well-behaved value, on a throwing\n/// value, and with `trytop` already at JS_TRYLIMIT.\n#[test]\nfn t_try_conversions_at_limit() {\n    with_big_stack(body_t_try_conversions_at_limit);\n}\n\nfn body_t_try_conversions_at_limit() {\n    let list: Vec<Mk> = vec![\n        Mk::Js(\"1.5\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"'abc'\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"undefined\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"({toString:function(){throw 'TS!'}})\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"({valueOf:function(){throw 'VO!'}})\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"Object.create(null)\"),\n        Mk::Js(\"({})\"),\n        Mk::Nat(29),\n    ];\n    // 62..66 straddles JS_TRYLIMIT (64); one js_try per nested js_pcall\n    for depth in [0i32, 1, 60, 61, 62, 63, 64, 66] {\n        let list = list.clone();\n        for flags in [0, JS_STRICT] {\n            diff2(\n                &format!(\"trylimit depth={depth} flags={flags}\"),\n                move |l| unsafe {\n                    let j = new_state(l, flags);\n                    let names = build_shapes(l, j, &list);\n                    install(l, j, Some(cf_try), REG_TRY);\n                    let mut s = String::new();\n                    for (i, n) in names.iter().enumerate() {\n                        NAME_A.with(|c| c.set(n.as_ptr()));\n                        DEPTH.with(|c| c.set(depth));\n                        out_push(format!(\"shape{i}\\n\").as_bytes());\n                        s.push_str(&format!(\"s{i} {}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_TRY)));\n                    }\n                    l.js_freestate(j);\n                    s\n                },\n            );\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/* ========================================== row 159 + out-of-range indices */\n\n/// Row 159 plus row 45: every predicate over every value shape, at in-range\n/// (positive and negative) and out-of-range indices.\n#[test]\nfn t_predicates() {\n    let list = shapes_full();\n    diff2(\"predicates\", move |l| unsafe {\n        let j = new_state(l, 0);\n        // leave every shape on the stack, at BOT-relative index i\n        let n = list.len() as c_int;\n        for m in &list {\n            build_one(l, j, m);\n        }\n        let mut s = format!(\"built {n}\\n\");\n        let mut idxs: Vec<c_int> = (0..n).collect();\n        idxs.extend((1..=n).map(|i| -i));\n        idxs.extend([n, n + 1, n + 500, -(n + 1), -(n + 500), 4100, -4100]);\n        for idx in idxs {\n            let mut bits = String::new();\n            for name in PREDS {\n                bits.push(if l.pred(name, j, idx) != 0 { '1' } else { '0' });\n            }\n            // row 163's sibling: js_isuserdata with a matching tag, a\n            // non-matching tag, and (only where the value is provably not\n            // userdata, see the file header) a NULL tag\n            let ua = l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, UD_A);\n            let ub = l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, UD_B);\n            let um = l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, UD_MISS);\n            let unull = if ua == 0 && ub == 0 && um == 0 {\n                format!(\"{}\", l.js_isuserdata(j, idx, std::ptr::null()))\n            } else {\n                \"skip\".to_string()\n            };\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"{idx}: {bits} ud={ua}{ub}{um}/{unull} t={} ty={}\\n\",\n                l.js_type(j, idx),\n                from_c(l.js_typeof(j, idx))\n            ));\n        }\n        s.push_str(&format!(\"gettop={}\\n\", l.js_gettop(j)));\n        l.js_freestate(j);\n        s\n    });\n}\n\n/* ======================================================= rows 169-182 */\n\n/// One comparison over one pair of registry-parked shapes.\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_cmp(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    l.js_getregistry(j, NAME_A.with(|c| c.get()));\n    l.js_getregistry(j, NAME_B.with(|c| c.get()));\n    let op = OP.with(|c| c.get());\n    let r: String = match op {\n        0 => {\n            OKAY.with(|c| c.set(-1));\n            let ok = OKAY.with(|c| c.as_ptr());\n            let v = l.js_compare(j, ok);\n            format!(\"compare={} okay={}\", v.signum(), OKAY.with(|c| c.get()))\n        }\n        1 => format!(\"equal={}\", l.nullary_i(\"js_equal\", j)),\n        2 => format!(\"strictequal={}\", l.nullary_i(\"js_strictequal\", j)),\n        3 => format!(\"instanceof={}\", l.nullary_i(\"js_instanceof\", j)),\n        4 => {\n            l.nullary(\"js_concat\", j);\n            format!(\n                \"concat top={} v={} repr={:?}\",\n                l.js_gettop(j),\n                vdesc(l, j, -1),\n                from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR))\n            )\n        }\n        _ => \"?\".to_string(),\n    };\n    out_push(format!(\"  {r} top={} a={} b={}\\n\", l.js_gettop(j), {\n        let t = l.js_gettop(j);\n        if t >= 2 {\n            slot(l, j, -2)\n        } else {\n            \"<gone>\".to_string()\n        }\n    }, {\n        let t = l.js_gettop(j);\n        if t >= 1 {\n            slot(l, j, -1)\n        } else {\n            \"<gone>\".to_string()\n        }\n    })\n    .as_bytes());\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n}\n\n/// Rows 169-182: `js_compare` (including the `okay` out-parameter), `js_equal`,\n/// `js_strictequal`, `js_instanceof` and `js_concat` over the full cross product\n/// of the shape subset.\n#[test]\nfn t_comparisons() {\n    let list = shapes_cross();\n    for flags in [0, JS_STRICT] {\n        let list = list.clone();\n        diff2(&format!(\"comparisons flags={flags}\"), move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, flags);\n            let names = build_shapes(l, j, &list);\n            install(l, j, Some(cf_cmp), REG_CMP);\n            let mut s = String::new();\n            for (ia, na) in names.iter().enumerate() {\n                for (ib, nb) in names.iter().enumerate() {\n                    NAME_A.with(|c| c.set(na.as_ptr()));\n                    NAME_B.with(|c| c.set(nb.as_ptr()));\n                    for op in 0..=4u32 {\n                        OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n                        out_push(format!(\"{ia}x{ib}o{op}\\n\").as_bytes());\n                        s.push_str(&format!(\"{ia}x{ib}o{op} {}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_CMP)));\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            s\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n/* ============================================================ row 168 */\n\n/// Row 168: `js_torepr(J, idx)` pushes the repr and then\n/// `js_replace(J, idx < 0 ? idx-1 : idx)`, i.e. it overwrites the slot it was\n/// asked about. An out-of-range `idx` makes that `js_replace` raise\n/// js_error \"stack error!\" (jsrepr.c:268-273), so it must be protected.\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_torepr(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    for k in 0..4 {\n        l.js_pushnumber(j, 10.0 + k as f64);\n    }\n    l.js_pushliteral(j, LIT_15);\n    l.js_newarray(j);\n    out_push(format!(\"  pre {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)).as_bytes());\n    let idx = A0.with(|c| c.get());\n    let op = OP.with(|c| c.get());\n    let r = if op == 0 {\n        format!(\"torepr={:?}\", from_c(l.js_torepr(j, idx)))\n    } else if op == 1 {\n        format!(\"tryrepr={:?}\", from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, idx, ERRSTR)))\n    } else {\n        l.js_repr(j, idx);\n        format!(\"repr pushed={:?}\", from_c(l.js_tostring(j, -1)))\n    };\n    out_push(format!(\"  {r}\\n  post {}\\n\", stack_snap(l, j)).as_bytes());\n    l.js_pushundefined(j);\n}\n\n/// Rows 164/168: `js_repr` / `js_torepr` / `js_tryrepr` and which stack slot\n/// each of them touches, over in-range and out-of-range indices.\n#[test]\nfn t_repr_replace() {\n    for op in 0..3u32 {\n        for idx in [-9i32, -7, -6, -3, -1, 0, 1, 5, 6, 7, 9] {\n            let tag = format!(\"repr op={op} idx={idx}\");\n            diff2(&tag, move |l| unsafe {\n                let j = new_state(l, 0);\n                install(l, j, Some(cf_torepr), REG_OP);\n                OP.with(|c| c.set(op));\n                A0.with(|c| c.set(idx));\n                let r = run(l, j, REG_OP);\n                l.js_freestate(j);\n                r\n            });\n        }\n    }\n\n    // and the self-referential / cyclic cases (row 166) at top level\n    for src in [\n        \"var o={}; o.self=o; o\",\n        \"var a=[1]; a.push(a); a\",\n        \"var a=[]; a[0]=a; a[1]=a; a\",\n        \"var o={a:{b:{}}}; o.a.b.top=o; o\",\n        \"new Error('boom')\",\n        \"var e=new Error(); delete e.message; e\",\n        \"var e=new Error('x'); e.name=''; e\",\n        \"var e=new Error('x'); e.name={toString:function(){return 'N'}}; e\",\n    ] {\n        diff2(&format!(\"cycle {src}\"), move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, 0);\n            let cs = cstr(src);\n            let rc = l.js_ploadstring(j, FILENAME, cs.as_ptr());\n            let mut s = format!(\"load={rc}\");\n            if rc == 0 {\n                l.js_pushundefined(j);\n                let rc = l.js_pcall(j, 0);\n                s.push_str(&format!(\" call={rc} repr={:?}\", from_c(l.js_tryrepr(j, -1, ERRSTR))));\n                l.js_pop(j, 1);\n            } else {\n                l.js_pop(j, 1);\n            }\n            s.push_str(&format!(\" top={}\", l.js_gettop(j)));\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            s\n        });\n    }\n}\n\n/* =================================================== row 56: cfunctiondata */\n\n/// Reports `js_currentfunction` / `js_currentfunctiondata` for a callee built\n/// by `js_newcfunctionx` (so `u.c.data` is really set) and for one built by\n/// `js_newcfunction` (data NULL).\nunsafe extern \"C\" fn cf_data(j: JS) {\n    let l = cur();\n    l.js_currentfunction(j);\n    let mut s = format!(\n        \"  curfn={} callable={} typeof={}\",\n        slot(l, j, -1),\n        l.pred(\"js_iscallable\", j, -1),\n        from_c(l.js_typeof(j, -1))\n    );\n    l.js_pop(j, 1);\n    let d = l.js_currentfunctiondata(j);\n    s.push_str(&format!(\" data_is_ud={}\\n\", d == ud_data()));\n    out_push(s.as_bytes());\n    l.js_pushnumber(j, 5.0);\n}\n\n/// Row 56 in detail: `js_currentfunctiondata` for a JS_CCFUNCTION with and\n/// without `data`, and at BOT == 0.\n#[test]\nfn t_currentfunctiondata() {\n    for withdata in [false, true] {\n        diff2(&format!(\"cfdata {withdata}\"), move |l| unsafe {\n            let j = new_state(l, 0);\n            if withdata {\n                l.js_newcfunctionx(j, Some(cf_data), PNAME, 0, ud_data(), None);\n            } else {\n                l.js_newcfunction(j, Some(cf_data), PNAME, 0);\n            }\n            l.js_setregistry(j, REG_CF);\n            let mut s = String::new();\n            // BOT == 0\n            l.js_currentfunction(j);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\"top-level curfn={}\\n\", vdesc(l, j, -1)));\n            l.js_pop(j, 1);\n            s.push_str(&format!(\n                \"top-level data_null={}\\n\",\n                l.js_currentfunctiondata(j).is_null()\n            ));\n            // and through a call\n            s.push_str(&format!(\"{}\\n\", run(l, j, REG_CF)));\n            // also as a method call from JS, so the callee reaches BOT-1 via\n            // the interpreter rather than via js_pcall\n            l.js_getregistry(j, REG_CF);\n            l.js_setglobal(j, PNAME);\n            let src = cstr(\"print(probe(), probe.call(1,2), [1,2].map ? 'x' : 'y')\");\n            let rc = l.js_dostring(j, src.as_ptr());\n            s.push_str(&format!(\"dostring={rc}\\n\"));\n            l.js_freestate(j);\n            s\n        });\n    }\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6730,"cache_read_input_tokens":141951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6730,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019QRhGRL5oyKghdRTM5wVAm","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"15eb0f31-7561-4aa5-bc92-362194c9499e","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:52:15.043Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write api_stack differential tests"}
