{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8a7968983ed02fe4","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019QRhGRL5oyKghdRTM5wVAm","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-0eE2Fw-translated-rust/a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2/tasks/a8a7968983ed02fe4.output","summary":"Done. `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test api_stack` passes with **13 tests, 0 failures**, confirmed on two consecutive runs (~2.1s each).\n\n## What was created\n\nOne new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/api_stack.rs` (1644 lines, 13 tests). Every call goes through the `.so` exports via the harness; no Rust function is called directly.\n\nInfrastructure worth noting:\n- `diff2` runs a closure against both libs and compares the full transcript, reporting a window around the **first differing line** (transcripts run to megabytes).\n- `stack_snap` / `snap_at` dump the *entire* observable stack: `js_gettop` plus `js_type`/`js_typeof`/predicates/value bits/`js_tryrepr` at every positive index, every negative index, and a 7-index out-of-range ring. `js_tryrepr` is applied to a `js_copy` because `js_torepr` ends in `js_replace(idx<0?idx-1:idx)` (jsrepr.c:271) and would rewrite the slot.\n- `strtag` separates **JS_TSHRSTR / JS_TLITSTR / JS_TMEMSTR** without reading the tag: `jsV_tostring` returns a pointer *into the stack slot* for SHRSTR, the caller's own pointer for LITSTR, and the `js_String` payload for MEMSTR, so a `js_copy` changes the pointer only for SHRSTR. Cross-checked against the `js_gc(J,1)` string counts.\n- Value shapes (152 for conversions/predicates, 48 for the cross product) are parked in the registry so any frame can re-push the *exact* `js_Value`, tag included. They cover every `js_Type` and every `js_Class` including JS_CSCRIPT (via `js_ploadstring` without calling), JS_CITERATOR, JS_CARGUMENTS, JS_CUSERDATA, JS_CMATH, JS_CJSON.\n\n## CONFIGS rows covered\n\n- **41-54** — `t_stack_ops_random` (120 seeded sequences × 20-80 ops, whole stack compared after **every** step; ops chosen from the *legal* set so rows 51/52/53 hit their exact 2/3/4-value boundary), `t_stack_errors`, `t_frames_and_currentfunction`.\n- **43/47/49** — `t_stack_errors`: 19 indices × 3 frame shapes × `js_pop`/`js_remove`/`js_replace`/`js_copy`/`js_rot`, all inside `js_pcall` so BOT>0 makes the `idx < BOT` arm reachable.\n- **50** — `t_insert_never_implemented`: 44 (idx, stack-shape) combos, all `(new Error(\"not implemented yet\"))` in both libs, always in a protected call.\n- **55** — `t_push_limits`: CHECKSTACK(1) via `js_pushnumber`/`js_copy`/`js_dup` and CHECKSTACK(2) via `js_dup2`.\n- **56** — `t_frames_and_currentfunction`: `js_currentfunction`/`js_currentfunctiondata` at BOT==0, in nested frames (depth 0/1/3), with `js_newcfunction` (data NULL) and `js_newcfunctionx` (same `data` pointer passed to both libs so equality is comparable), plus via `js_dostring`.\n- **57-70 (+71-73)** — `t_pushes_and_strings` (300+ bodies incl. lengths 0-20/30-32/63-65, embedded NULs, random ascii/unicode/raw bytes) and `t_push_values_and_new` (774 doubles, `js_pushboolean` over INT_MIN/INT_MAX/64 random ints, all 38 native builders).\n- **142-158** — `t_conversions`: 152 shapes × 22 entry points × {0, JS_STRICT}, pre/post slot state recorded (catches `js_tostring`-on-number and `js_toobject`-on-primitive in-place mutation).\n- **159** — `t_predicates`: 17 predicates + `js_isuserdata`×4 tags over 152 shapes at 311 indices.\n- **160-162** — `t_conversions` + `t_try_conversions_at_limit` (nested `js_pcall` depths 0/1/60-64/66 straddling JS_TRYLIMIT).\n- **163** — `js_touserdata` (right tag / wrong tag / non-userdata) and `js_toregexp` in `t_conversions`.\n- **164-168** — `t_repr_family`: `js_repr`/`js_torepr`/`js_tryrepr` at 11 indices × 3 entry points showing exactly which slot each touches, plus cycles, holes, errors with/without `message`, and escaping.\n- **169-182** — `t_comparisons`: 48×48 cross product × {`js_compare` (with the `okay` out-param), `js_equal`, `js_strictequal`, `js_instanceof`, `js_concat`} × 2 flag settings, each in its own protected call; includes a callable rhs whose `prototype` is `1` and `Function.prototype` (callable, no `prototype` property) for row 181's two typeerrors.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** The Rust translation matched the C byte-for-byte on every case.\n\nTo prove the tests are not vacuous I temporarily injected three mutations into `src/jsrun.rs` (`js_pushboolean` dropping `!!v`; `js_pushstring`'s SHRSTR threshold `<=` → `<`; a wrong source slot in `js_rot3`) and confirmed 5 tests failed. All three were reverted with surgical edits; `src/jsrun.rs` is byte-identical to its pre-mutation content and `target/debug/.src_hash` is unchanged at `33ecfc68023115a1` (same value as the first build of the session). `tests/smoke.rs` also still passes. **No `src/*.rs` changes were needed or kept.**\n\n## Deliberately excluded (C undefined behaviour, documented in the file header with file:line)\n\n`js_pop` with `n<0` (jsrun.c:403, raises TOP into uninitialised slots); the whole unchecked `js_dup`/`js_dup2`/`js_rot2-4`/`js_rot2pop1`/`js_rot3pop2` family and `js_rot(n>gettop)` below their value requirement (jsrun.c:442-498, indexes before the array start when BOT==0); indices near `INT_MIN` (jsrun.c:220 signed overflow); `js_pushlstring` with `n<0` or `n==JS_STRLIMIT` (jsrun.c:163); `js_isuserdata(..., NULL)` over an actual userdata (jsrun.c:266 `strcmp(NULL,...)`); and `js_currentfunctiondata` with a JS_CFUNCTION at BOT-1 (jsrun.c:211 — noted as unreachable through the public API rather than UB, since jsproperty.c:167 memsets the object).","usage":{"total_tokens":287042,"tool_uses":90,"duration_ms":1787229},"uuid":"f6ebba6d-1a07-4fca-8faa-26da2c5d7b21","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2"}
