{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01XAVh8gZWfhUpSQSS9fpjD2","type":"tool_result","content":"# SYMBOLS.md — exported-symbol parity (C `libmujs.so` vs Rust `libmujs.so`)\n\nGenerated mechanically with `nm -D --defined-only` on both shared objects\n(`c_src/build/libmujs.so` and `target/debug/libmujs.so`).\n\n## Totals\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| symbols exported by C `.so` | 237 |\n| symbols exported by Rust `.so` | 237 |\n| **C symbols MISSING from Rust `.so`** | **0** |\n| extra symbols only in Rust `.so` | 0 |\n| undefined **non-libc** symbols in Rust `.so` | **0** |\n\nEvery undefined entry in the Rust `.so` is a libc / libgcc import\n(`malloc`, `realloc`, `memcpy`, `memset`, `_setjmp`, `longjmp`, `pow`, `sin`,\n`gmtime`, `mktime`, `snprintf`, `_Unwind_*`, ...). The C `.so` imports the same\nset plus `ceil`/`floor`/`fmod`/`sqrt`/`__assert_fail`; the Rust build lowers\nthose four to instructions instead of libm calls.\n\n### Note: variadic and macro-generated symbols\n\nThe 8 printf-style variadic entry points (`js_error`, `js_evalerror`,\n`js_rangeerror`, `js_referenceerror`, `js_syntaxerror`, `js_typeerror`,\n`js_urierror`, `jsC_error`) cannot be written as C-variadic functions in stable\nRust. They are exported from `src/lib.rs` as `#[naked]` x86-64 SysV\ntrampolines (`va_trampoline!`) that materialise a `va_list` and tail into the\n`*_va` worker in `src/jserror.rs` / `src/jscompile.rs`. The\n`js_new*error` family is generated by the `DERROR!` macro in `src/jserror.rs`.\nThose are the rows whose \"Rust module\" column reads `lib.rs (naked va)` or\n`jserror.rs (DERROR! macro)`.\n\n## Per-symbol table\n\n| # | symbol | defined in (C) | in Rust `.so` | Rust module |\n|---|--------|----------------|---------------|-------------|\n| 1 | `jsB_init` | jsbuiltin.c | YES | jsbuiltin.rs |\n| 2 | `jsB_initarray` | jsarray.c | YES | jsarray.rs |\n| 3 | `jsB_initboolean` | jsboolean.c | YES | jsboolean.rs |\n| 4 | `jsB_initdate` | jsdate.c | YES | jsdate.rs |\n| 5 | `jsB_initerror` | jserror.c | YES | jserror.rs |\n| 6 | `jsB_initfunction` | jsfunction.c | YES | jsfunction.rs |\n| 7 | `jsB_initjson` | json.c | YES | json.rs |\n| 8 | `jsB_initmath` | jsmath.c | YES | jsmath.rs |\n| 9 | `jsB_initnumber` | jsnumber.c | YES | jsnumber.rs |\n| 10 | `jsB_initobject` | jsobject.c | YES | jsobject.rs |\n| 11 | `jsB_initregexp` | jsregexp.c | YES | jsregexp.rs |\n| 12 | `jsB_initstring` | jsstring.c | YES | jsstring.rs |\n| 13 | `jsB_propf` | jsbuiltin.c | YES | jsbuiltin.rs |\n| 14 | `jsB_propn` | jsbuiltin.c | YES | jsbuiltin.rs |\n| 15 | `jsB_props` | jsbuiltin.c | YES | jsbuiltin.rs |\n| 16 | `jsC_compilefunction` | jscompile.c | YES | jscompile.rs |\n| 17 | `jsC_compilescript` | jscompile.c | YES | jscompile.rs |\n| 18 | `jsC_error` | jscompile.c | YES | lib.rs (naked va) |\n| 19 | `jsP_freeparse` | jsparse.c | YES | jsparse.rs |\n| 20 | `jsP_parse` | jsparse.c | YES | jsparse.rs |\n| 21 | `jsP_parsefunction` | jsparse.c | YES | jsparse.rs |\n| 22 | `jsR_newenvironment` | jsrun.c | YES | jsrun.rs |\n| 23 | `jsR_unflattenarray` | jsrun.c | YES | jsrun.rs |\n...\n73:| 36 | `jsV_delproperty` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n74:| 37 | `jsV_getownproperty` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n75:| 38 | `jsV_getproperty` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n76:| 39 | `jsV_getpropertyx` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n77:| 40 | `jsV_newiterator` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n80:| 43 | `jsV_nextiterator` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n87:| 50 | `jsV_resizearray` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n88:| 51 | `jsV_setproperty` | jsproperty.c | YES | jsproperty.rs |\n90:| 53 | `jsV_toboolean` | jsvalue.c | YES | jsvalue.rs |\n91:| 54 | `jsV_tointeger` | jsvalue.c | YES | jsvalue.rs |\n92:| 55 | `jsV_tonumber` | jsvalue.c | YES | jsvalue.rs |\n93:| 56 | `jsV_toobject` | jsvalue.c | YES | jsvalue.rs |\n94:| 57 | `jsV_toprimitive` | jsvalue.c | YES | jsvalue.rs |\n95