{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a53a5768ccd537970","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VmbNeb2udNwZDvRGXHnnSV","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-0eE2Fw-translated-rust/a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2/tasks/a53a5768ccd537970.output","summary":"Done. Here's the report.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/err_core.rs`** — 4889 lines, **58 tests**, `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_core` passes with 0 failures (verified twice in a row, plus 8 extra back-to-back runs after fixing one flake). The full suite (12 test files / 292 tests) also passes.\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/cov_err_core.tsv`** — 258 lines, one per ERRORS.md row.\n\n## Coverage: 243 of rows 1-258 covered; 15 uncoverable\n\n| row(s) | why not coverable |\n|---|---|\n| 40 | `jsrun.c:541` `js_pushrune(rune<0)` unreachable — `js_utflen` (jsstring.c:49) and `js_runeat` (jsstring.c:20) use *identical* rune accounting (astral = 2 positions, stop at NUL), so every `k` in `[0, u.s.length)` is addressable. Boundary still diffed by `t_string_wrapper_indices`. |\n| 41 | `jsR_unflattenarray`'s `js_try` handler sets `properties = NULL`; every later `lookup`/`jsG_scanobject`/`jsG_freeobject` then NULL-derefs. UB. |\n| 49, 50, 52 | live `assert()`s in the *static* `jsR_setarrayindex`; both call sites pre-check `simple && k>=0 && k<=flat_length`. |\n| 51 | needs `flat_length >= 1<<26` = 1 GiB of flat array data (grows one element at a time). Reachable sibling `jsrun.c:708` is covered. |\n| 66 | `jsrun.c:792` unreachable: reached only when `!own`, and `jsV_setproperty` then returns either a fresh `atts=0` node or NULL (same `lookup` that made `own==0`). |\n| 101 | `jsR_savescope` overflow unreachable: `envtop <= tracetop` is invariant, and `jsR_pushtrace`'s `==` check (row 105) always fires first. Measured limit: depth **1021**. |\n| 108 | unreachable given row 107 (ERRORS.md says so too). |\n| 143 | `js_tryboolean`'s setjmp path: `jsV_toboolean` is a total switch, cannot throw. Its `js_ptry` half (row 142) *is* covered. |\n| 147, 148 | build-time asserts, always true; `t_shrstr_boundary` shows the tag really is at byte 15. |\n| 218 | `assert(!simple)` in `jsV_resizearray`; guarded at its only in-library call site, and the Rust carries no `assert!`s (matches `-DNDEBUG`), so driving it would be a deliberate non-input divergence. `t_resizearray` drives it on non-simple arrays. |\n| 256 | `100*gtot/ntot` with `ntot==0` unreachable from `js_newstate` (R/G/GE/builtins always exist). `t_gc_sweep_report` asserts `ntot>0`. |\n| 257 | GC report line max 62 + 11×11 = 183 bytes. |\n\n## Divergences found: **none**\n\n`src/*.rs` is byte-identical to what I started with (`src_hash` still `33ecfc68023115a1`); no `Edit` was applied to any `src/` file.\n\nTo prove the tests aren't passing vacuously I ran two mutation rounds against `src/` and reverted them:\n- `\"not implemented yet\"` → `\"not implemented\"` and `vsnprintf(...,256,...)` → `200` in `jserror.rs`: killed by `t_stack_manip_errors` and `t_error_varargs_ffi`.\n- 6 further message/format mutations (`'%s' is read-only or non-configurable`, `on transient object`, `object is non-extensible`, `not an iterator`, `[object]`, the GC report format): killed by **15** tests.\n- `CHECKSTACK`'s `>=` → `>` segfaults (the mutation is itself UB), so it was reverted rather than kept.\n\n## Notable things verified rather than assumed\n\n- The four bare-string throws really are `JS_TLITSTR`: `ty=string, iserror=0, e instanceof Error === false, typeof e.message === 'undefined'` for `\"stack overflow\"`, `\"out of memory\"`, `\"script ran too long\"`, `\"exception stack overflow\"`.\n- Value stack capacity is identical (4093 pushes from a cfunction frame) in both libraries; a `cap-N` sweep plus progress breadcrumbs proves row 124 (`OP_GETLOCAL`'s CHECKSTACK) is the specific site that trips at `cap-2`.\n- The naked-asm varargs trampolines were exercised with 34 distinct real C-varargs shapes per thrower × 7 throwers: 0 args, GP spill (10 pointers / 12 ints), SSE spill (10-12 doubles), interleaved GP+SSE spill, `%ld`/`%lld`, `%.*s`/`%*d`, `NULL %s` → `(null)`, and 255/256-byte truncation.\n- Row 81 (`jsR_defproperty`'s readonly label with neither `strict` nor `throw`) is only reachable through `js_initvar` against a `with` scope object — `with([1,2,3]) { eval('var length') }` silently drops the declaration in both libraries.\n- Row 125 (`OP_GETLOCAL`'s non-lightweight ReferenceError) needs the Bug-701886 skip in `jsR_callscript`: `this.b = 1; eval('var b; delete b; b')`.\n- `js_pushvalue`'s 16-byte `js_Value` really is classified INTEGER,INTEGER (confirmed by `objdump`: it reads `%rsi`/`%rdx`), so it is called across the FFI as `fn(JS, u64, u64)`.\n- An asymmetry worth knowing: `js_tryrepr` (jsrepr.c:278) installs its handler with a bare `js_try` and **no** `js_ptry` guard, unlike `js_trystring` (jsstate.c:50) — so at `trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT` it throws instead of returning the default. `vshape_notry` exists in the test file for exactly that reason.\n- `js_pconstruct` computes `savetop = TOP - n - 2` while `js_construct` wants the callee at `-n-1`, so its error path writes one slot *below* the callee; `t_call_paths` keeps two guard slots underneath so the write stays in memory we own (with an empty stack it would be `STACK[-1]`, so that is not tested).\n\nI deliberately did **not** touch `ERRORS.md`'s `cov` column — sibling agents own rows 259-933 of the same file and concurrent writes would race; the TSV is the merge input.","usage":{"total_tokens":474523,"tool_uses":175,"duration_ms":3796434},"uuid":"9e4fbf21-f4a8-4b01-a79b-9e42606f7ace","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2"}
