{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aa60f3f3173049c3f","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011t8iFLHMb5bgoLacPAhX39","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-0eE2Fw-translated-rust/a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2/tasks/aa60f3f3173049c3f.output","summary":"Done. `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_builtin` passes with **0 failures twice in a row** (verified twice again after a concurrent edit to another agent's `tests/err_misc.rs`).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/err_builtin.rs`** — 57 `#[test]` functions (194 KB), all driven through the two `.so` exports.\n- **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/cov_err_builtin.tsv`** — 254 lines, one per ERRORS.md row 477-730.\n\n## Coverage: 247 / 254 rows\n\nError rows assert the exact constructor name **and** exact message text (`expect_exprs` / `expect_bodies` / `ok_str`), not just \"both failed\"; behaviour-fork rows assert byte-identical transcripts. JS-level probes run inside `js_ploadstring`+`js_pcall` plus a JS `try`, FFI-level probes inside the `cfunction`+`js_pcall` probe pattern — nothing can throw at `trytop == 0`. No test writes to stdout, so the file-local `STDOUT_LOCK` is present but unused (documented).\n\nHighlights: all 17 `checkstring` sites × null/undefined × `.call`/`.apply` + coercible + throwing-`toString` receivers; every `js_toobject(J,0)` entry point separately (message distinct from `checkstring`'s); digit/radix sweeps one step past every bound in both directions; `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` both sides via `js_setlength`, `new Array(n)` and `Ap_push`; `regexec failed` through all four `jsstring.c` call sites (`with_big_stack`); the two URIErrors plus explicit proof that lone surrogates and malformed UTF-8 raise **no** error (JS and raw-byte FFI); `Op_toString` on all 16 `js_Class` values including `JS_CSCRIPT`/`JS_CITERATOR`/`JS_CUSERDATA`; rows 493/604/605 with one shared real `1<<28`-byte buffer; ten `js_try` cleanup handlers reached by exhausting `J->memlimit`.\n\n## The 7 uncovered rows\n\n| row | reason |\n|---|---|\n| 484 | Unreachable: `stack[BOT-1]` always `JS_TOBJECT` (`js_iscallable` gates every `jsR_pushtrace`; `jsR_callcfunction` only overwrites the slot after `F` returns; `trace[0]` never examined) |\n| 486 | Unreachable: `fun == Ap_join` implies that frame's own `Ap_join_cycle` already ran `js_toobject(J,0)`, which rewrites the slot in place |\n| 500 | UB: `jsarray.c:279` reads `u.object`/`u.a.*` with no type or class check — for `JS_CSTRING` a heap *address* is reinterpreted as `flat_length` (nondeterministic). Only zero-initialised `JS_COBJECT` receivers driven |\n| 614 | UB: `jsstring.c:254` frees uninitialised `p` |\n| 637 | UB: signed overflow needs >536M args; `JS_STACKSIZE == 4096` forbids it. Reachable half (no RangeError) is covered |\n| 650, 664 | Dead call sites (`static`, gated by `js_isregexp`). `TypeError \"not a regexp\"` pinned on the exported `js_toregexp`, and the gate itself pinned |\n\n## Divergences found and fixed: **none**\n\nThe Rust translation matched the C on every one of these ~254 rows. To prove the tests are not passing vacuously I ran 13 targeted mutations of `src/*.rs` (`x > 10`→`>= 10` in `Sp_replace_regexp`, `JS_READONLY`→`JS_DONTENUM` in `ToPropertyDescriptor`, `width > 20`→`>= 20`, `radix > 36`→`> 37` in both `Np_toString` and `jsB_parseInt`, `len <= 1`/`len == limit`/`i == a && k == n`, both `hasOwnProperty` index bounds, `Ap_join_cycle`'s `return 0`, `Ap_sort_cmp`'s two-holes exit, `Decode`'s reserved test, `istrim`, `js_utflen`'s `rune >= 0x10000`); **all 11 whose pattern matched were caught**, and every mutation was reverted (`src/*.rs` content hash verified back to `33ecfc68023115a1`).\n\n## Notes worth passing on\n\n- Two C behaviours ERRORS.md describes incorrectly (tests assert the real behaviour): rows 545/601 say the C-function result is read as `this` when nothing is pushed — `jsR_callcfunction`'s `if (TOP > save_top)` (jsrun.c:1266) substitutes **`undefined`**, so `'abc'.concat()` is `undefined`. Row 545's `switch` default is also dead: `enum js_Class` has exactly the 16 enumerated members.\n- Several inputs had to be excluded as C signed-overflow UB, each documented at the test: `len + from` in `Ap_indexOf`/`Ap_lastIndexOf` for negative `length` with `fromIndex == INT_MIN` (gcc wraps and `lastIndexOf` then loops 2^31 times), and `k = len - 1` in `Ap_reduceRight` for `{length: -1e30}`.\n- `tests/err_misc.rs` (another agent's file, edited at 14:01 during my session) has 2 failing tests, `t_repr_sparse_array` and `t_repr_throwing_getter` — jsrepr.c rows, outside 477-730 and not touched by me.\n- I did **not** fill in the `cov` column of `ERRORS.md`; it is shared with the agents owning other row ranges and the coverage map is the stated deliverable.","usage":{"total_tokens":396726,"tool_uses":129,"duration_ms":4096500},"uuid":"32c8a8da-78df-490e-b728-dc57162e2769","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011t8iFLHMb5bgoLacPAhX39","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_builtin` passes with **0 failures twice in a row** (verified twice again after a concurrent edit to another agent's `tests/err_misc.rs`).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/err_builtin.rs`** — 57 `#[test]` functions (194 KB), all driven through the two `.so` exports.\n- **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/cov_err_builtin.tsv`** — 254 lines, one per ERRORS.md row 477-730.\n\n## Coverage: 247 / 254 rows\n\nError rows assert the exact constructor name **and** exact message text (`expect_exprs` / `expect_bodies` / `ok_str`), not just \"both failed\"; behaviour-fork rows assert byte-identical transcripts. JS-level probes run inside `js_ploadstring`+`js_pcall` plus a JS `try`, FFI-level probes inside the `cfunction`+`js_pcall` probe pattern — nothing can throw at `trytop == 0`. No test writes to stdout, so the file-local `STDOUT_LOCK` is present but unused (documented).\n\nHighlights: all 17 `checkstring` sites × null/undefined × `.call`/`.apply` + coercible + throwing-`toString` receivers; every `js_toobject(J,0)` entry point separately (message distinct from `checkstring`'s); digit/radix sweeps one step past every bound in both directions; `JS_ARRAYLIMIT` both sides via `js_setlength`, `new Array(n)` and `Ap_push`; `regexec failed` through all four `jsstring.c` call sites (`with_big_stack`); the two URIErrors plus explicit proof that lone surrogates and malformed UTF-8 raise **no** error (JS and raw-byte FFI); `Op_toString` on all 16 `js_Class` values including `JS_CSCRIPT`/`JS_CITERATOR`/`JS_CUSERDATA`; rows 493/604/605 with one shared real `1<<28`-byte buffer; ten `js_try` cleanup handlers reached by exhausting `J->memlimit`.\n\n## The 7 uncovered rows\n\n| row | reason |\n|---|---|\n| 484 | Unreachable: `stack[BOT-1]` always `JS_TOBJECT` (`js_iscallable` gates every `jsR_pushtrace`; `jsR_callcfunction` only overwrites the slot after `F` returns; `trace[0]` never examined) |\n| 486 | Unreachable: `fun == Ap_join` implies that frame's own `Ap_join_cycle` already ran `js_toobject(J,0)`, which rewrites the slot in place |\n| 500 | UB: `jsarray.c:279` reads `u.object`/`u.a.*` with no type or class check — for `JS_CSTRING` a heap *address* is reinterpreted as `flat_length` (nondeterministic). Only zero-initialised `JS_COBJECT` receivers driven |\n| 614 | UB: `jsstring.c:254` frees uninitialised `p` |\n| 637 | UB: signed overflow needs >536M args; `JS_STACKSIZE == 4096` forbids it. Reachable half (no RangeError) is covered |\n| 650, 664 | Dead call sites (`static`, gated by `js_isregexp`). `TypeError \"not a regexp\"` pinned on the exported `js_toregexp`, and the gate itself pinned |\n\n## Divergences found and fixed: **none**\n\nThe Rust translation matched the C on every one of these ~254 rows. To prove the tests are not passing vacuously I ran 13 targeted mutations of `src/*.rs` (`x > 10`→`>= 10` in `Sp_replace_regexp`, `JS_READONLY`→`JS_DONTENUM` in `ToPropertyDescriptor`, `width > 20`→`>= 20`, `radix > 36`→`> 37` in both `Np_toString` and `jsB_parseInt`, `len <= 1`/`len == limit`/`i == a && k == n`, both `hasOwnProperty` index bounds, `Ap_join_cycle`'s `return 0`, `Ap_sort_cmp`'s two-holes exit, `Decode`'s reserved test, `istrim`, `js_utflen`'s `rune >= 0x10000`); **all 11 whose pattern matched were caught**, and every mutation was reverted (`src/*.rs` content hash verified back to `33ecfc68023115a1`).\n\n## Notes worth passing on\n\n- Two C behaviours ERRORS.md describes incorrectly (tests assert the real behaviour): rows 545/601 say the C-function result is read as `this` when nothing is pushed — `jsR_callcfunction`'s `if (TOP > save_top)` (jsrun.c:1266) substitutes **`undefined`**, so `'abc'.concat()` is `undefined`. Row 545's `switch` default is also dead: `enum js_Class` has exactly the 16 enumerated members.\n- Several inputs had to be excluded as C signed-overflow UB, each documented at the test: `len + from` in `Ap_indexOf`/`Ap_lastIndexOf` for negative `length` with `fromIndex == INT_MIN` (gcc wraps and `lastIndexOf` then loops 2^31 times), and `k = len - 1` in `Ap_reduceRight` for `{length: -1e30}`.\n- `tests/err_misc.rs` (another agent's file, edited at 14:01 during my session) has 2 failing tests, `t_repr_sparse_array` and `t_repr_throwing_getter` — jsrepr.c rows, outside 477-730 and not touched by me.\n- I did **not** fill in the `cov` column of `ERRORS.md`; it is shared with the agents owning other row ranges and the coverage map is the stated deliverable."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa60f3f3173049c3f (use SendMessage with to: 'aa60f3f3173049c3f', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 397492\ntool_uses: 129\nduration_ms: 4096502</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2","uuid":"391f3b68-2fec-4894-b4ea-3a9189cf2670","timestamp":"2026-08-23T14:02:31.798Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Work in /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust\n\nCONTEXT\nC->Rust translation of MuJS, verified by DIFFERENTIAL TESTING against the C.\n`c_src/` is the ground truth: READ-ONLY, never modify it and never create any\nfile under it. `src/*.rs` is the Rust translation built as a cdylib.\n\nCRITICAL BUILD RULE\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib (the tests reach it only via dlopen).\nALWAYS run `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_builtin`. Bare `cargo test`\nafter editing src/ trips a \"STALE Rust cdylib\" assertion. Never bypass it.\n\nREAD FIRST\n  ERRORS.md            - the error-surface table (933 rows). YOUR ROWS ARE 477-730.\n  tests/common/mod.rs  - the harness\n  tests/err_core.rs    - a large existing Phase-C example in exactly the wanted\n                         style (protected-call probes, UB documentation, and a\n                         STDOUT_LOCK for anything that writes to stdout)\n  tests/js_builtins.rs - existing valid-path builtin tests\n\nHARNESS API\n  libs() -> &'static Pair { c: Lib, rs: Lib }\n  new_state(l, flags) -> JS ; set_cur(l)\n  eval / dostring / diff_eval / diff_dostring\n  Lib::<every exported symbol>, l.pred(name, j, idx), l.nullary, l.raw2::<T>(name)\n  cstr / from_c / out_clear / out_take / Rng::new(seed) / with_big_stack(fn_item)\n\nYOUR TASK: PHASE C for ERRORS.md rows 477-730\n(jsarray.c 477-539, jsobject.c 540-589, jsstring.c 590-679, jsnumber.c 680-711,\n jsboolean.c 712-715, jsbuiltin.c 716-730)\n\nCreate ONE new file `tests/err_builtin.rs`. For EVERY row in that range write a\ndifferential test that constructs that exact invalid input, calls BOTH\nlibraries, and asserts they return the SAME error - identical message text and\nerror constructor name, not merely \"both failed\".\n\nRead the C first. Things to get exactly right:\n  - `checkstring` (jsstring.c:15) has 17 call sites, all producing TypeError\n    \"string function called on null or undefined\". Drive EACH String.prototype\n    method with `this` = null and undefined (via .call/.apply), and assert the\n    message. Then also drive each with a non-string coercible `this`.\n  - `js_toobject(J, 0)` on undefined/null gives TypeError \"cannot convert\n    undefined to object\" / \"cannot convert null to object\" (jsvalue.c:401-402).\n    Every Np_*, Bp_*, Sp_toString/valueOf and Op_hasOwnProperty/isPrototypeOf/\n    propertyIsEnumerable reaches it. Cover each entry point separately - the\n    message differs from checkstring's and a translation could confuse them.\n  - Number.prototype.toFixed / toExponential / toPrecision digit-range\n    RangeErrors, and Number.prototype.toString radix range. Sweep the digit\n    counts and radices one step past each documented bound in BOTH directions,\n    and with NaN / Infinity / fractional / negative / non-numeric arguments.\n  - Array length: RangeError \"invalid array length\" and \"array too large\" are\n    raised at jsrun.c:707/709 and jsrun.c:676, reached from jsarray.c:19\n    (js_setlength) and jsarray.c:31 (the single-numeric-arg Array constructor).\n    JS_ARRAYLIMIT is 1<<26. Drive both sides of the boundary.\n  - The URI state machines in jsbuiltin.c: URIError \"truncated escape sequence\"\n    (jsbuiltin.c:145) and \"invalid escape sequence\" (jsbuiltin.c:149) are the\n    ONLY URIErrors possible - Encode/Decode work on raw bytes and never validate\n    UTF-8 well-formedness, so the ES5 lone-surrogate URIErrors are absent. Assert\n    that: feed lone surrogates and malformed sequences and confirm NO error.\n  - Op_toString (jsobject.c:27) has a `switch (self->type)` with no `default`:\n    an unenumerated class pushes nothing and the result is read off the stack\n    top. Check which classes reach it before testing.\n  - jsstring.c:605 `if (x > 10)` (should be `>= 10` per spec): an out-of-range\n    `$10` backreference emits `':'`. Reproduce the C, do not fix it.\n  - Every remaining explicit range/bounds check, NULL check, and\n    `return -1`/`return NULL`/`return 0` failure signal in those six files.\n\nALSO cover generic FFI boundary abuse for the entry points these files export:\nNULL `const char *` arguments, zero and oversized lengths, values one step past\neach documented range, and OUT-OF-RANGE ENUM/int values across the FFI.\n\nRULES\n  - Every call must go through the harness (through the .so exports). Never call\n    Rust functions directly.\n  - MANY randomized inputs where a row has a value dimension, fixed seed.\n  - NEVER call a throwing entry point outside a protected context\n    (js_pcall/js_pconstruct/js_ploadstring/js_dostring). Use the cfunction-probe\n    pattern from tests/err_core.rs. A throw with trytop==0 aborts the process.\n  - Some C paths are UNDEFINED BEHAVIOUR. Do NOT test those; add a `///` comment\n    naming file:line and why. Ones already known:\n      * jsstring.c:573 Sp_replace_regexp's FUNCTION-replacement arm walks\n        `m.sub[x].sp` past the end when all 15 capture groups participate -> both\n        libraries SIGSEGV. Cap that variant at 13 groups.\n      * jsarray.c:279/:365 Ap_sort_cmp/Ap_sort_swap read u.a.simple/u.a.array\n        without a class check, so Array.prototype.sort.call(nonArray, ...) reads\n        a never-stored union member.\n      * jsstring.c:253-258 Sp_substring_imp's js_try handler frees an\n        uninitialised `p` (OOM only).\n      * jsstring.c:455 S_fromCharCode's `(top-1)*UTFmax+1` can overflow int.\n    Verify each against the C before relying on my summary.\n  - If ANY test writes to stdout (js_gc(J,1), js_trap via `debugger`,\n    jsS_dumpstrings), it must hold a file-local STDOUT_LOCK for its whole\n    duration - see tests/err_core.rs. Otherwise the suite is flaky.\n  - Keep each test under ~60s.\n\nDELIVERABLE 2: write a coverage map to\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/cov_err_builtin.tsv\none line per ERRORS.md row 477-730:\n  <row number>\\t<test function name>\nor for rows you could not cover:\n  <row number>\\tUNCOVERABLE: <reason>\n\nIF YOU FIND A DIVERGENCE\nThe C is ALWAYS right. Fix `src/*.rs` with the Edit tool (surgical edits only --\nnever Write over an existing src file). Re-read the C and make the Rust match.\n\nFINISH ONLY WHEN `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_builtin` passes with 0\nfailures twice in a row. Report: number of tests, how many of rows 477-730 are\ncovered, the uncoverable ones with reasons, and every divergence found+fixed.","agentId":"aa60f3f3173049c3f","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_builtin` passes with **0 failures twice in a row** (verified twice again after a concurrent edit to another agent's `tests/err_misc.rs`).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- **`/local