{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ae61ca1db3605c181","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014EJrrhqixnoaGuQ4YBud4x","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-0eE2Fw-translated-rust/a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2/tasks/ae61ca1db3605c181.output","summary":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n`timeout 600 ./run_tests.sh --test err_misc` — **62 tests, 0 failures, twice in a row** (8.6 s per run).\n\n**Deliverable 1:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/translated_rust/tests/err_misc.rs` (4097 lines, 62 `#[test]`s).\n**Deliverable 2:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-0eE2Fw/tmp/vwork/cov_err_misc.tsv` — 203 lines, one per ERRORS.md row 731-933.\n\n## Coverage\n198 of 203 rows driven by a differential test that asserts the *exact* error string / sentinel (not merely \"both failed\"). All 32 regexp.c `die()` sites get their own pattern, including each of the 4 `\"unmatched '('\"` sites, all 4 `\"unterminated escape sequence\"` sites, both `\"invalid quantifier\"` sites and both reachable `\"program too large\"`/`\"numeric overflow\"` sites. Every limit is driven from below to above one step at a time (REPINF at 255, REG_MAXCLASS at 129, REG_MAXSPAN at the 32nd span, REG_MAXSUB at the 16th group, `count()` recursion at 4097 chars, `strlen*2` at 16385 bytes, whole-program size, and the `regexec` -1 flip at 4095/4097 depending on shape). Allocation failures (rows 757/759/763/764) use `js_regcompx` with a fail-at-*k* allocator and compare the **full callback log** (order + requested sizes) as well as the message. Only 3 tests need `with_big_stack`; the rest run on the normal stack (14 concurrent 512 MB threads exhausted VM).\n\n## Uncoverable (5), each verified against the C\n- **761** regexp.c:942 `\"syntax error\"` — `parsecat`/`parsealt` can only return with the lookahead at EOF or `)`, and :939 catches `)`.\n- **788** regexp.c:1221 `default:` — unreachable without memory corruption; `emit()` only writes valid opcodes, every `pc` target is later filled, and `count()` never under-counts what `compile()` emits.\n- **888 / 889** jsfunction.c:145/169 `n < 0` — `__BoundArguments__` is always the array `Fp_bind` built, defined `READONLY|DONTENUM|DONTCONF`. `t_function_bound_calls` proves it can't be replaced, deleted or given a negative length (the attempt raises `RangeError: invalid array length`).\n- **909** jsrepr.c:262 `sb ? sb->s : \"undefined\"` — dead code; :261 runs `js_putc(J,&sb,0)` first and `js_putc` allocates when `*sbp == NULL`.\n\nNot tested, documented as UB in the file header: `js_regcomp(pattern=NULL)` (`strlen` of NULL at regexp.c:920), `js_regexec(prog=NULL)` (regexp.c:1235), `js_regexec(sp=NULL)`. `sub=NULL` *is* defined and is tested.\n\n## Divergences found\n**None.** `src/*.rs` is byte-identical to what I started with (`.src_hash` still `33ecfc68023115a1`); no fix was needed. To prove the suite is not passing vacuously I temporarily perturbed `jsU_runelen` in `src/utf.rs` and confirmed `t_utf_runelen_sentinels` failed with `jsU_runelen(0x0): left 2, right 3`, then reverted.\n\n## Notable C behaviours reproduced verbatim\n- `jsrepr.c:129` sparse-array holes → asserted against literals like `\"[1, , 3]\"`, `\"[1, 2, ]\"`, `\"[, , ]\"`.\n- `jsrepr.c:231` `\"[iterator \"` with no closing `]` (driven via `js_pushiterator` from a protected cfunction; the `[userdata mytag]` sibling *is* balanced).\n- `jsdate.c:748` `setUTCHours` defaulting minutes from `HourFromTime` instead of `MinFromTime`.\n- `js_Regexp::last` being `unsigned short`: `lastIndex = 70000` reads back 4464, `-1` reads back 65535.\n- Three `strchr` int→char truncation quirks in regexp.c I had to work around and then documented as tests: `\\u0131` is accepted as an identity escape because `strchr(ESCAPES, 305)` matches `'1'`; inside a class, an escape whose low byte is `0x00` matches `strchr`'s terminating NUL and one whose low byte is `d/s/w/D/S/W` takes the shorthand arm, adding **no span**.\n- `strncmpcanon` counting BYTES as runes: `(?=.(é))\\1` on `\"éé\"` no-matches with `REG_ICASE` (row 792) but *matches* without it, since plain `strncmp` compares bytes.\n\n## Harness hardening added\n`diff_script` wraps `diff_dostring` with a non-vacuity guard: the script must reach completion (`rc == 0`), must not hit the report hook, must emit ≥ 5 lines, and must contain no `(eval):` SyntaxError or `ReferenceError`. That guard immediately caught 5 of my own generated fragments that were silently failing to parse identically in both libraries (bare `function(){}` / `{length:1,0:'a'}` passed to `eval`, and a reference to the non-existent `escape`), so those cases now actually exercise the rows they were written for.","usage":{"total_tokens":383611,"tool_uses":152,"duration_ms":4631763},"uuid":"9c3205e3-620b-47fd-8b9b-91f5b4b1efe0","session_id":"a62d17ad-8528-487e-8b6a-23ad0ded9ac2"}
