and `--all-features` |\n\n**411 differential tests, 0 failures**, ~31k lines across 14 test files. Every call crosses the FFI boundary via `libloading` into *both* `.so` files — the Rust `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are exercised exactly as an external caller would.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed (all in `src/jsrun.rs`)\n\nThree cases of **C unspecified argument-evaluation order**, which gcc x86-64 resolves right-to-left. `js_toobject()` rewrites the stack slot in place (`jsvalue.c:410`), so the order is observable:\n\n1. `js_setproperty` (`jsrun.c:1011`) — `js_isobject` must run *before* `js_toobject`, or a primitive receiver is not flagged `transient`, silently creating properties on a throwaway wrapper instead of raising `\"cannot create property 'x' on transient object\"`.\n2. `js_setindex` (`jsrun.c:1049`) — same defect.\n3. `js_defaccessor` (`jsrun.c:1028`) — setter resolved first, then getter, then `js_toobject`; decides which of three TypeErrors fires.\n\nI confirmed each against `objdump` of the C `.so` rather than trusting the sub-agent's report — e.g. `js_setproperty` calls `js_isobject@plt` at `2bf01` and `js_toobject@plt` at `2bf1a`.\n\n## Two harness bugs worth flagging\n\n- **`cargo test` never rebuilds the cdylib** (test targets reach it only via `dlopen`), so early runs were testing a **stale `.so` and passing vacuously**. Mutation testing exposed this. Fixed with `run_tests.sh` + an mtime *and* content-hash guard in the harness; I verified the guard fires by backdating a mutated source.\n- **Mutation testing was essential.** The first sweep showed 10 modules whose mutations survived. `tests/gaps.rs` closes those; the suite now kills a deliberate mutation in **all 26** Rust modules.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `c_src/` is untouched (31 source files, no added files). Its `.so` isn't linked against libm, so the harness `dlopen`s libm `RTLD_GLOBAL` first — and must leak it, since `dlclose` removes it from the global scope again.\n- Genuine C UB is documented rather than tested (each with `file:line`): `js_fmtexp` writes `se[9]` for 10-digit exponents; `js_strtol` with `base > 80` runs off the buffer; `js_pushlstring` with `n < 0` loops ~2^64 times; `Sp_replace_regexp` reads `m.sub[16]` with 15 participating groups.\n- `ll_regexp.rs` takes ~172 s of the ~4 min total (catastrophic-backtracking cases at the `REG_MAXREC` boundary).","ttft_ms":2766,"ttft_stream_ms":2599,"time_to_request_ms":105,"type":"result","duration_ms":24057340,"uuid":"d4296753-3ffa-4f24-97d5-d21189039ef9"}
